#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""load-watch: find the agent behind a sustained load spike, tell it, and steer that work to CI (free GitHub runners; Forgejo/Hyades for MIT/SIPB work). No model.

    load-watch sample [--dry-run] [-v]      one sample (launchd runs this every 20 s); also watches compressor churn
    load-watch status                       streak, top consumers in the window, cooldowns
    load-watch incidents [-n N]             the incident ledger, newest last
    load-watch ack ID "what you did"        the agent's answer to a brief (recorded in the ledger)
    load-watch ci list|check DIR|rm DIR       the CI-first decisions `bg` reads
    load-watch ci decide DIR ci "CI CMD"|local "why"|pending "note"
    load-watch ci-only list|add DIR "CMD"|rm DIR|check DIR   (older form of `ci`, kept for scripts)
    load-watch guard status|list|add LABEL [KEY=VALUE...] [--note N]|rm LABEL|reset LABEL
    load-watch admit [--max-per-core N] [--max-mem-churn N] [--min-free-mb N] [--max-pageins N] [--max-agents [N]] [--no-reserve]
    load-watch renew RESERVATION             extend an agent reservation by LW_RESERVE_S from now (a dispatcher still waiting)
    load-watch release RESERVATION           shorten an agent reservation `admit --max-agents --json` printed (its agent is spawned)
                     [--boost-per-core N] [--boost-max-churn N] [--wait SECONDS] [--json]
                                            may new work START now? exit 0 yes, 75 still too hot, 2 usage
    load-watch watcher set [--paseo ID|--relay T] [--name N] [--chain C]|show [--json]|clear [T]|test [TEXT]
                                            the one session told about every spike (`loadwatch` skill)
    load-watch install|uninstall            the launchd job (launchd/com.djbclark.load-watch.plist)

Why (2026-10-18): agents keep starting heavy builds and tests on this 8-core Mac (load 24-41 that
morning; 180 on 2026-10-13, 300-400 on 2026-10-04). `bg`, `heavy-shim` and the Claude test hook throttle
what goes through them; nothing noticed what did not, or told the agent that started it. Plektra and
stayturgid-agent already build only on CI (free GitHub runners since 2026-10-18, `ci/base` + `ci/run/**`; `forgejo-ci` skill); this finds the next
candidate.

Each sample is one `ps` call and `os.getloadavg()`: no model, no network. A sample counts as hot when
the 1-minute load per core is at least LW_LOAD_PER_CORE (4.0; was 2.0 until 2026-11-01, when djbclark called 3.5 per core "not too bad for this system": on this 16 GB, 8-core Mac the real limit is memory pressure and process churn, not the load average). After LW_SUSTAIN_S (300) seconds of
continuously hot samples it attributes the mean CPU of the samples in that window to sessions (session-finder's fleet.py; a process belongs
to the session whose pid is its ancestor, a daemonised one such as a Gradle daemon to the only session
in its git repo) and, for each session above LW_MIN_CORES (1.5) cores, writes a brief, types one line
naming it into the session (relay.py), and sends one hermes-ping (with a ready `acp-dispatch cursor` line for a fixer when the relay fails). A session or repo is not told again
for LW_COOLDOWN_H (6) hours (by session, and by the repos its processes worked in). The brief names the
work's own repo, not the session's cwd (2026-10-18, `work_repos`): each top process's cwd, else its nearest
ancestor's (brew and cargo children run in temp dirs), mapped to a git top-level, with that repo's `ci` decision,
its Forgejo remote and whether an ancestor was `bg` (and which exception let it through: release or targeted
test). Several repos are listed with their share of the cores; with none mapped it falls back to the session's
cwd and says that is a guess. That lsof/ancestor work runs only when a brief is written, never per sample.
The agent is asked to finish what is running (never to kill paid-for
work), ask djbclark before creating a CI copy of a repo that is not on GitHub, and, once CI runs, `load-watch ci-only add`
the repo so `bg` refuses local builds and tests in it.

Job guard (2026-10-18): each sample also checks launchd jobs (see the `job guard` section): a crash loop in
any non-Apple job (20 failed restarts in 10 min, or 60 in 2 h), and hangs, CPU, memory or run time in the jobs listed in ~/.config/load-watch/guard.tsv.
A trip boots the job out, kills its processes, pings Hermes and cools it down 90 min, then re-tests it; a
5th round in 24 h disables it for good (`load-watch guard reset LABEL` brings it back). Events: guard.jsonl.

Load watcher (djbclark, 2026-10-20): `watcher set` registers one agent session (the `loadwatch` skill does it;
a Paseo agent by `paseo send`, anything else by relay.py). Every incident, every sustained load no agent
explains, and every guard trip is also sent to it, so a session with a model investigates. One record
(watcher.json): `set` replaces the last watcher and tells it so. A failed send is stamped `last_fail`, never
fatal (2026-10-23: a Paseo send that fails with the exact code DAEMON_UNREACHABLE, DAEMON_CONNECTION_LOST, DAEMON_NOT_READY or
DAEMON_NOT_RUNNING, a daemon restart, is retried twice, 5 s apart, inside 30 s, and once one send has given up the
rest of that process make one attempt each; any other failure and the relay channel get one attempt); the watcher is skipped for an incident only when it is the blamed session and the relay reached it.
Unexplained sustained load reaches the watcher at most hourly (WATCHER_NOCPU_S), Hermes every LW_COOLDOWN_H.

Compressor churn (2026-10-23, djbclark's memory-thrash follow-up): `admit` only refuses to START work while the
compressor thrashes; running work and anything that skips `bg`/`acp-dispatch` stayed invisible. Each sample
therefore reads macOS `vm_stat` Compressions + Decompressions once, takes the delta against the previous
sample's counter (kept in state.json as churn_prev / churn_prev_t; no extra sleep, so the first sample, a
counter that went backwards, a gap over MAX_GAP_S and a missing `vm_stat` give no reading) and keeps
`churn_since` while pages/s stay above ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S (the admit limit). Held for LW_CHURN_SUSTAIN_S (180)
seconds it sends one line, with the top 3 commands by cores, to the watcher at most hourly (cooldown
`churn-watcher`, WATCHER_NOCPU_S) and to Hermes every LW_COOLDOWN_H (cooldown `churn`); `status` lists both.
When a top command matches Grok|Chrome|WindowServer the line adds the loadwatch skill's standing exception;
the alert itself is never suppressed. No incident row, nothing is signalled or killed; --dry-run prints and
records nothing. Test hook: LW_FAKE_COMPRESSOR (a comma list of cumulative counters, one per read, the last
repeating; set, it replaces vm_stat, `admit` ignores it).

State: ~/.local/state/load-watch/ (state.json, incidents.jsonl, guard.jsonl, briefs/, sample.log, watcher.json).
Registry: ~/.config/load-watch/ci-only.tsv (repo TAB mode TAB CI command or reason TAB date), read by `bg`
through `load-watch ci check`. CI-first (djbclark, 2026-10-18): every repo `bg` builds in needs a decision.
`ci`: `bg` refuses and names the CI command. `local`: runs here, with the reason (macOS-only, ...).
`pending`: runs here but `bg` reminds the agent to investigate (repos seeded from 7 days of `bg` use).
No row: `bg` refuses (exit 3) until the agent investigates offloading (GitHub runners: `forgejo-ci` skill section 6 item 6) and decides.
A git worktree or cow pasture with no row of its own takes its main repo's row; a key ending in `/*`
covers every repo under that directory. Older 3-column rows (repo, CI command, date) read as `ci`.
Admission (operator, 2026-10-19): `admit` is the dispatcher-facing predicate acp-dispatch calls before it
launches a slice (`--load-wait`, `--no-load-gate`). It reads os.getloadavg()[0] / os.cpu_count() and says
`admit ok load1=X per_core=Y cores=N` (exit 0) when the per-core load is at most --max-per-core (default
1.5; `bg`'s own base is 2.5 since 2026-11-01 and it passes that; the 4.0 boost below usually decides, and LW_LOAD_PER_CORE is only this watcher's blame step), else
`admit hot ...` (exit 75, EX_TEMPFAIL). When state.json is fresh the line also carries the watcher's
`streak` and `hot_for_s`, so a sustained-hot machine reads as such. `--wait 0` (default) is a pure check;
`--wait S` polls every 15 s for up to S seconds, prints one line per waited minute to stderr, and once the
load drops below the threshold sleeps a random 5-30 s, never past --wait (so queued dispatchers do not all start together)
and re-checks. `--json` prints one JSON object with the same fields. It only decides whether to START work:
it never kills, throttles or signals anything. Memory gate (operator 2026-10-23, "your recommended is fine"; tightened 2026-11-01):
`admit` samples macOS `vm_stat` twice, 2 s apart, and says no (exit 75) while ANY of these holds: free + speculative
memory is below --min-free-mb (default 600, env LW_MIN_FREE_MB); compressor churn (Compressions + Decompressions, pages/s)
exceeds --max-mem-churn (default 20000, env LW_MAX_COMPRESSOR_S; 60000 until 2026-11-01); pageins exceed --max-pageins per
second (default 1000, env LW_MAX_PAGEINS_S: macOS `Pageins` also counts file-backed reads, so read-heavy work can trip it
with memory to spare; that errs toward waiting); or, ONLY when the caller passes --max-agents (acp-dispatch does; `bg` never
does: a test run starts no agent, and gating it would starve the very sessions the cap counts), the live `acp-run` slices
machine-wide (one `ps`, exact argv match of the process running the script named acp-run, never pgrep/pkill -f) number
N or more (bare --max-agents = 14, env LW_MAX_AGENTS, 0 = no cap: THE knob to tune how many acp-run slices may START);
an admission under the cap is recorded as a reservation (agent-reservations.json, flock) counted with the live ones for
until `load-watch release ID` (acp-dispatch does it at spawn) or LW_RESERVE_S (1200), so concurrent dispatchers cannot all
pass at 13 of 14 (--no-reserve: records none but still counts the held ones; LW_RESERVE_S=0: off). A
vm_stat or ps that exists but fails, times out or prints nonsense refuses too (`memory_unreadable`, `agents_unreadable`):
that is likeliest when the machine is starving. Only an absent tool (Linux without vm_stat, no /proc) leaves its gate open,
listed in `unreadable`. Why, measured 2026-11-01 (load watcher d8891c91):
load 35-70 on this 8-core, 16 GB Mac was memory starvation, not CPU: ~64 MB free, ~12k compressions+decompressions/s,
~1760 pageins/s, kernel_task 57% and sys 25-39% of CPU, 31+ live agent processes (omp 20, copilot 11, claude 8, agy 3); the
4.0 calm boost let a slice start in every brief dip and each start pushed memory back over. The 2026-10-23 calibration of
the churn line (215 ten-second samples: calm tail 11-22k, load 10-25 p50 49k, load >=25 p50 80k and p90 108k pages/s) set
60000; 2026-11-01 showed starvation at 12k, so it is 20000. Load and swap alone did not separate that spike from a calm hour.
Runaway Chrome (operator 2026-10-25): the sample step tells the watcher (never kills) when one Google Chrome process
(not "Chrome for Testing") has used LW_CHROME_CORES (0.9) or more for LW_CHROME_SUSTAIN_S (300), once an hour per pid, with its kind, the
URL on its command line when it has one, and role-aware Task Manager (Shift+Esc) advice: match the pid and
report the task; a browser/GPU alert does not identify a busy tab. Only an identified tab may be ended by the operator.
Calm boost (operator 2026-10-25): while churn is known and at most --boost-max-churn (default = the compressor limit, 20000; 25000 until 2026-11-01)
the per-core limit is --boost-per-core (default 4.0, was 2.0 until 2026-11-01; 0 turns it off) instead of --max-per-core, even when a caller such as `bg`
passes its base; at higher churn, or when churn cannot be read, the base limit holds. Hysteresis (2026-11-01): the boost
applies only after the machine has stayed calm (churn at most the boost line, free memory above the floor, pageins under
their limit) for LW_BOOST_CALM_S (600) seconds without a break; any hot reading, by `admit` or by the 20 s `sample` step,
resets the clock (calm.json in the state dir, written atomically; a gap over 120 s between readings also restarts it; the
result's `calm_for_s` and `status` show the run). The result and `--json` `max_per_core` are the
limit in force. Swap is not the signal (86-92% in calm hours too). The result and the `--json`
record carry `mem_churn_pages_s`, `free_mb`, `pageins_s`, `agents` and `refused` (the names of the gates that said no: load,
compressor, free_mem, pageins, agents); a reading that cannot be taken is listed in `unreadable` and its gate stays open
(Linux reads /proc/meminfo MemAvailable and /proc/vmstat pswpin+pswpout and pgmajfault as the equivalents). Test hooks
(acp-dispatch scrubs them from the environment it gives admit): LW_FAKE_LOAD1 (a load, or a comma list read one per poll
with the last value repeating), LW_FAKE_CHURN, LW_FAKE_FREE_MB, LW_FAKE_PAGEINS, LW_FAKE_AGENTS (the same for each reading;
a faked load leaves the readings it does not fake healthy: churn 0, 8192 MB free, 0 pageins, 0 agents),
LW_ADMIT_POLL_S (15, floored at 1), LW_ADMIT_STAGGER_S ("5,30" min,max; 0 <= min <= max <= 60). A state.json
that is not a dict with numeric `t` and `hot_since` counts as no state. Non-finite --wait or --max-per-core: exit 2.
Exit: 0 ok, 1 nothing found (check, ack of an unknown id), 2 usage; `admit` also 75 (still too hot).
"""
import argparse
import json
import math
import os
import random
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

HOME = Path.home()
ADE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
SF = ADE / "skills" / "session-finder"
STATE_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("LW_STATE_DIR", HOME / ".local/state/load-watch"))
REGISTRY = Path(os.environ.get("LW_REGISTRY", HOME / ".config/load-watch/ci-only.tsv"))
PLIST = ADE / "launchd" / "com.djbclark.load-watch.plist"
LABEL = "com.djbclark.load-watch"
HERMES_PING = HOME / ".local/bin/hermes-ping"

LOAD_PER_CORE = float(os.environ.get("LW_LOAD_PER_CORE", "4.0"))  # was 2.0 until 2026-11-01 (operator: 3.5 per core is not too bad)
SUSTAIN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_SUSTAIN_S", "300"))  # seconds of continuous hot load
MAX_GAP_S = 900  # a longer gap between samples is a sleep, not load
MIN_CORES = float(os.environ.get("LW_MIN_CORES", "1.5"))
COOLDOWN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_COOLDOWN_H", "6")) * 3600
WATCHER_NOCPU_S = 3600  # the watcher is told of unexplained sustained load at most this often
MY_UID = os.getuid()
STUCK = []  # commands ps saw in state U this sample
PSTATE = {}  # pid -> (ps state, rss in KB) this sample, for the job guard
BGRUN = []  # commands runnable at background priority this sample


def now():
    return time.time()


def stamp(t=None):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(t or now()))


def log(msg):
    STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(STATE_DIR / "sample.log", "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{stamp()} {msg}\n")


def load_state():
    try:
        return json.loads((STATE_DIR / "state.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {"samples": [], "streak": 0, "cooldown": {}}


def save_state(st):
    STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = STATE_DIR / "state.json.tmp"
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(st))
    tmp.replace(STATE_DIR / "state.json")


def ps_table():
    """pid -> (ppid, uid, cores now, command), one ps call. `%cpu` is the kernel's decayed recent share, so a
    snapshot every 20 s averages to an unbiased per-process estimate, short-lived compilers included (a
    `time` difference misses every process that starts and exits between samples, and macOS `ps -S` does
    not fold exited children into the parent: checked 2026-10-18)."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-axo", "pid=,ppid=,uid=,%cpu=,state=,pri=,rss=,command="], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, timeout=20).stdout
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:  # the machine is stalling (2026-10-18, load 77): skip this sample
        return None
    table = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        parts = line.split(None, 7)
        if len(parts) < 7 or not parts[0].isdigit():
            continue
        cmd = parts[7] if len(parts) > 7 else ""
        PSTATE[parts[0]] = (parts[4], int(parts[6]) if parts[6].isdigit() else 0)
        if parts[4].startswith("U"):  # uninterruptible wait: counts in load, uses no CPU
            STUCK.append(cmd[:80] or parts[0])
        # runnable at background QoS (priority 4: E-cores only, throttled). A pile of these is load with idle
        # P-cores: 2026-10-18's load 110 was orphaned agent-radar scans at background QoS.
        if parts[4].startswith("R") and parts[5] == "4":
            BGRUN.append(" ".join(os.path.basename(w) for w in cmd.split()[:2])[:60])
        try:
            table[parts[0]] = (int(parts[1]), int(parts[2]), float(parts[3]) / 100, cmd)
        except ValueError:
            continue
    return table


def window(st):
    """pid -> [cores summed over the kept samples, uid, command], and the number of samples (so sum / n is the
    mean)."""
    use = {}
    for s in st["samples"]:
        for pid, (cores, uid, cmd, _) in s["d"].items():
            row = use.setdefault(pid, [0.0, uid, cmd])
            row[0] += cores
    return use, len(st["samples"])


def ppids(st, table):
    """pid -> ppid, from the window's samples (processes that have exited since) and the current table."""
    out = {pid: r[3] for s in st["samples"] for pid, r in s["d"].items()}
    out.update({pid: row[0] for pid, row in table.items()})
    return out


def git_top(path):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", path, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=5)
        return r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else ""
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""


def proc_cwd(pid):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["lsof", "-a", "-p", str(pid), "-d", "cwd", "-Fn"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=5)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""
    return next((ln[1:] for ln in r.stdout.splitlines() if ln.startswith("n")), "")


def attribute(use, span, parent):
    """Group the window's CPU by session. Returns (per-session dicts, unattributed rows)."""
    sys.path.insert(0, str(SF))
    import fleet  # noqa: E402  (session-finder; ~2 s, so only on a sustained spike)
    sessions = [s for s in fleet.sessions() if s.get("pid")]
    by_pid = {str(s["pid"]): s for s in sessions}
    tops = {}
    for s in sessions:
        tops.setdefault(git_top(s["cwd"]) if s.get("cwd") else "", []).append(s)
    groups, loose = {}, []
    for pid, (secs, uid, cmd) in sorted(use.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][0]):
        cores = secs / span if span else 0
        if cores < 0.1:
            break
        owner, p, hops = None, pid, 0
        while p and hops < 64:
            if p in by_pid:
                owner = by_pid[p]
                break
            p, hops = str(parent.get(p, "")), hops + 1
        if owner is None and uid == MY_UID and cores >= 0.5 and pid in parent:
            top = git_top(proc_cwd(pid) or "/")
            if top and len(tops.get(top, [])) == 1:
                owner = tops[top][0]
        row = {"pid": int(pid), "cores": round(cores, 2), "cmd": cmd[:300]}
        if owner is None:
            loose.append(row)
            continue
        g = groups.setdefault(owner["id"], {"session": owner, "cores": 0.0, "procs": []})
        if str(owner["pid"]) != pid:  # the TUI's own CPU is not build work
            g["cores"] += cores
            g["procs"].append(row)
    return groups, loose


def forgejo_remote(top):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", top, "remote", "-v"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""
    return next((ln.split()[1] for ln in r.stdout.splitlines() if "forgejo" in ln), "")


BG_REAL = os.path.realpath(HOME / "ops/site-djbclark/bin/bg")
BG_PATH = re.compile(r"(^|/)site-[^/]+/bin/bg$")
SHELLS = {"bash", "sh", "zsh", "env"}


def proc_cmds(st, table):
    """pid -> command, from the window's samples (processes that have exited since) and the current table."""
    out = {pid: r[2] for s in st["samples"] for pid, r in s["d"].items()}
    out.update({pid: row[3] for pid, row in table.items()})
    return out


def proc_cwds(pids):
    """pid -> working directory for every live pid in `pids`, one lsof call."""
    pids = sorted({str(p) for p in pids if p})
    if not pids:
        return {}
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["lsof", "-a", "-d", "cwd", "-Fpn", "-p", ",".join(pids)], capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return {}
    out, cur = {}, None
    for ln in r.stdout.splitlines():
        if ln.startswith("p"):
            cur = ln[1:]
        elif ln.startswith("n") and cur:
            out[cur] = ln[1:]
    return out


def bg_args(cmd):
    """The words after `bg` when `cmd` is a run of ops/site-*/bin/bg (the script or the interpreter running it),
    else None."""
    words = cmd.split()
    for i, w in enumerate(words[:4]):
        if w.endswith("/bin/bg") and (BG_PATH.search(w) or os.path.realpath(w) == BG_REAL) and (
                i == 0 or os.path.basename(words[i - 1]) in SHELLS or words[i - 1].startswith("-")):
            return words[i + 1:]
    return None


def bg_rule(args):
    """Which of bg's `ci`-mode exceptions (`ci_release`, `ci_targeted` in site-djbclark/bin/bg) these arguments
    match; '' when neither. A cheap re-reading of those rules, so a hint, not a verdict."""
    if "--local-tests" not in args:
        for i, a in enumerate(args):
            base = os.path.basename(a)
            if base == "release.py" or (base == "just" and next((x for x in args[i + 1:] if not x.startswith("-")),
                                                                  "").startswith(("release", "release-"))):
                return "release"
    if any(os.path.basename(a) in ("pytest", "py.test", "gradle", "gradlew") or a in ("pytest", "unittest")
           for a in args) and any(a.startswith(("-k", "--tests")) or "::" in a or re.search(r"test\w*\.py$", a)
                                  for a in args):
        return "targeted test"
    return ""


def work_repos(g, session_top, parent, cmds):
    """Where the group's processes really worked, for an incident brief only (lsof and git: never per sample).
    A process belongs to the repo of its own working directory, else of its nearest ancestor's (a brew or cargo
    child runs in a temp or build dir), stopping below the session's TUI. Whether an ancestor is `bg` is read
    from the same chain. 2026-10-18 incident 20261018-2056-82c4844a blamed the session's cwd for rustc under
    `brew reinstall`, started by `just release` in another repo through bg. Falls back to the session's repo,
    labelled a guess, when nothing maps."""
    owner = str(g["session"].get("pid") or "")
    procs = sorted(g["procs"], key=lambda p: -p["cores"])[:40]
    chains = {}
    for p in procs:
        chain, q = [], str(p["pid"])
        while q and q not in ("0", "1", owner) and len(chain) < 64:
            chain.append(q)
            q = str(parent.get(q, ""))
        chains[p["pid"]] = chain
    cwds = proc_cwds({q for c in chains.values() for q in c})
    tops = {}
    repos, unmapped = {}, 0.0
    for p in procs:
        chain = chains[p["pid"]]
        top = ""
        for q in chain:
            if cwds.get(q):
                tops.setdefault(cwds[q], git_top(cwds[q]))
                top = tops[cwds[q]]
                if top:
                    break
        args = next((a for a in (bg_args(cmds.get(q, "")) for q in chain) if a is not None), None)
        if not top:
            unmapped += p["cores"]
            continue
        r = repos.setdefault(top, {"top": top, "cores": 0.0, "bg_cores": 0.0, "rule": ""})
        r["cores"] += p["cores"]
        if args is not None:
            r["bg_cores"] += p["cores"]
            r["rule"] = r["rule"] or bg_rule(args)
    guess = not repos
    if guess and session_top:
        repos[session_top] = {"top": session_top, "cores": g["cores"], "bg_cores": 0.0, "rule": ""}
        unmapped = 0.0
    rows = registry()
    out = sorted(repos.values(), key=lambda r: -r["cores"])
    for r in out:
        r["ci"] = decision(r["top"], rows)[1]
        r["remote"] = forgejo_remote(r["top"])
    return {"repos": out, "unmapped": round(unmapped, 2), "guess": guess}


MODES = ("ci", "local", "pending")


def registry():
    """repo -> [mode, CI command or reason, date]."""
    rows = {}
    try:
        for ln in REGISTRY.read_text().splitlines():
            parts = ln.split("\t")
            if not parts or not parts[0] or parts[0].startswith("#"):
                continue
            if len(parts) > 1 and parts[1] in MODES:
                rows[parts[0]] = (parts[1:] + ["", ""])[:3]
            else:  # pre-2026-10-18 row: repo, CI command, date
                rows[parts[0]] = ["ci"] + (parts[1:] + ["", ""])[:2]
    except OSError:
        pass
    return rows


def write_registry(rows):
    REGISTRY.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = REGISTRY.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text("# repo top-level (or DIR/*)\tci|local|pending\tCI command, or why local\tdecided\n" +
                   "".join(f"{k}\t{v[0]}\t{v[1]}\t{v[2]}\n" for k, v in sorted(rows.items())))
    tmp.replace(REGISTRY)


def main_worktree(top):
    """The main checkout of a linked git worktree, else ''."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", top, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""
    common = r.stdout.strip()
    return os.path.dirname(common) if r.returncode == 0 and common.endswith("/.git") else ""


def pasture_source(top):
    """The checkout a cow pasture was made from (~/.cow/state.json records it), else ''."""
    try:
        pastures = json.loads((HOME / ".cow/state.json").read_text()).get("pastures") or []
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return ""
    return next((p.get("source") or "" for p in pastures if isinstance(p, dict) and p.get("path") == top), "")


def decision(top, rows):
    """(key, row) deciding `top`: its own row, its main worktree's or pasture source's, or a DIR/* row."""
    for key in (top, main_worktree(top), pasture_source(top)):
        if key and key in rows:
            return key, rows[key]
    globs = [k for k in rows if k.endswith("/*") and (top + "/").startswith(k[:-1])]
    if globs:
        key = max(globs, key=len)
        return key, rows[key]
    return "", None


def repo_line(r):
    """One repo's Forgejo remote, CI decision and whether it ran under bg."""
    where = (f"It has a Forgejo remote: `{r['remote']}` (MIT/SIPB CI)." if r["remote"] else
             "It has no Forgejo remote (a GitHub-sourced repo uses GitHub runners).")
    mode, text = (r["ci"] or ["", ""])[:2]
    if r["bg_cores"] and r["bg_cores"] >= r["cores"] - 0.05:
        ran = "It ran under `bg`" + (f" (through bg's {r['rule']} rule)" if r["rule"] and mode == "ci" else "")
    elif r["bg_cores"]:
        ran = f"{r['bg_cores']:.1f} of its {r['cores']:.1f} cores ran under `bg`, the rest outside it"
    else:
        ran = "It ran outside `bg`"
    if mode == "ci":
        verdict = f"Registered CI-first (`ci`: `{text}`). {ran}" + (
            ", which lets a targeted test or a release through; if this was neither, tell djbclark." if r["bg_cores"]
            and not r["rule"] else "." if r["bg_cores"] else ", which refuses builds there; something bypassed it.")
    elif mode:
        verdict = f"Decision: `{mode}` ({text}). {ran}."
    else:
        verdict = f"No CI decision yet. {ran}."
    return f"{where} {verdict}"


def brief(inc, g, work, load1, ncpu):
    s = g["session"]
    procs = "\n".join(f"{i}. pid {p['pid']}, {p['cores']} cores: `{p['cmd'][:200]}`"
                      for i, p in enumerate(sorted(g["procs"], key=lambda p: -p["cores"])[:8], 1))
    repos, stop = work["repos"], s.get("cwd")
    if work["guess"]:
        r = repos[0] if repos else None
        where = (f"Repo (a guess: no process's working directory, nor its ancestors', is in a git repo, so this is "
                 f"the session's cwd): `{r['top']}`. {repo_line(r)}" if r else "The work ran outside any git repo.")
    elif len(repos) == 1:
        where = f"Repo (from the processes' working directories): `{repos[0]['top']}`. {repo_line(repos[0])}"
    else:
        where = ("The work ran in several repos (from the processes' working directories):\n\n" + "\n".join(
            f"{chr(96 + i)}. `{r['top']}`, {r['cores']:.1f} of those cores. {repo_line(r)}"
            for i, r in enumerate(repos, 1)))
    if not work["guess"] and work["unmapped"] >= 0.1:
        where += f"\n{work['unmapped']:.1f} cores ran in no git repo."
    if not work["guess"] and stop and all(not str(stop).startswith(r["top"]) for r in repos):
        where += f"\nYour session's cwd (`{stop}`) is outside {'it' if len(repos) == 1 else 'them'}."
    todo = [r for r in repos if (r["ci"] or [""])[0] not in ("ci", "local")]
    if todo:
        adds = "\n".join(f"   `~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/load-watch ci-only add {r['top']} \"<the command that runs it on CI>\"`"
                         for r in todo)
        step4 = f"""4. Once a CI job runs, register the repo so `bg` refuses heavy local runs and names your command:
{adds}"""
    else:
        step4 = ("4. Nothing to register: every repo above already has a decision (`ci` or `local`). If `bg` let "
                 "heavy work through that it should have refused, say so in your ack.")
    return f"""# load-watch incident {inc}

Written {stamp()} by `~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/load-watch` (no model). Load was {load1:.1f} on {ncpu} cores
(threshold {LOAD_PER_CORE} per core) for {SUSTAIN_S / 60:g}+ min, and your session
({s.get('agent')} `{s.get('name') or s['id']}`, cwd `{s.get('cwd')}`) used about {g['cores']:.1f} cores of it:

{procs}

{where}

## What to do

1. Finish the step you are on. Do not kill or restart running work to obey this (it is already paid for);
   just do not start another heavy local run of this kind.
2. Next time, run this kind of build or test on CI: load the `forgejo-ci` skill
   (`~/src/djbclark-ade/skills/forgejo-ci/SKILL.md`, section 6 item 6 is the recipe for a repo whose
   source of truth is on GitHub: an orphan `ci/base` branch with a workflow and a `scripts/github-*`
   wrapper that pushes `ci/run/<slug>` to free GitHub runners; Forgejo/Hyades only for MIT/SIPB work).
3. Pushing branches to a repo djbclark does not own, or creating a Forgejo repo, is outward-facing: ask
   djbclark first (one AskUserQuestion, or hermes-ping if no one is at your pane). Light work that
   cannot move (a single small test file) goes through `~/ops/site-private/bin/bg` instead.
{step4}
5. If you are a fresh agent dispatched on this brief, the session that ran the work is gone: djbclark
   dispatched you after agreeing to a CI copy, so steps 2-4 are yours.
6. Answer this brief in one line: `~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/load-watch ack {inc} "<what you did or plan>"`.
"""


def notify(inc, g, top, path, load1, ncpu, dry):
    s = g["session"]
    cmd = sorted(g["procs"], key=lambda p: -p["cores"])[0]["cmd"][:60] if g["procs"] else "the session itself"
    line = (f"load-watch {inc}: load {load1:.0f} on {ncpu} cores for {SUSTAIN_S / 60:g}+ min; your processes used "
            f"~{g['cores']:.1f} cores ({cmd}). After your current step, read {path} and act on it.")
    relayed = False
    if not dry:
        target = s.get("sid") or s["id"]
        try:
            # --no-defer: the brief is time-critical, so a busy session that cannot take it now is "could not reach it"
            # (the fixer line below), never "queued": a queued brief arrives after the load spike it is about
            r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(SF / "relay.py"), target, line, "--no-defer", "--no-ack"], capture_output=True,
                               text=True, timeout=60, env=relay_env())
            relayed = r.returncode == 0
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            pass
    who = f"{s.get('agent')} {s.get('name') or s['id']}"
    ping = (f"djbclark-ade: load-watch {inc}: {who} used ~{g['cores']:.1f} cores at load {load1:.0f} "
            f"({cmd}); {'told it' if relayed else 'could not reach it (' + (s.get('where') or 'no channel') + ')'};"
            f" brief {path}")
    if not relayed:  # the code-slice pick (route_agent.py plan, 2026-10-18); he runs it after a yes to a CI copy
        ping += (f"; to hand it to a fixer: ~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/acp-dispatch cursor --model default --kind code "
                 f"--name load-watch-{Path(path).stem} --task load-watch "
                 f"-C {top or s.get('cwd') or HOME} -f {path} --detach --no-wait")
    if not dry and HERMES_PING.exists():
        subprocess.run([str(HERMES_PING), ping], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
    return relayed, ping


# ---- the load watcher (djbclark, 2026-10-20) -------------------------------------------------------------
# One agent session at a time owns the load loop (the `loadwatch` skill registers it). It hears about every
# incident, every sustained load no agent explains, and every job-guard trip, on top of the blamed session and
# Hermes, so someone with a model investigates. One record, so there is never a second watcher: `set`
# replaces it and tells the one it replaced.

def watcher():
    try:
        w = json.loads((STATE_DIR / "watcher.json").read_text())
        return w if isinstance(w, dict) and w.get("target") and w.get("channel") in ("paseo", "relay") else None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def save_watcher(w):
    STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = STATE_DIR / "watcher.json.tmp"
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(w, indent=1) + "\n")
    tmp.replace(STATE_DIR / "watcher.json")


# A Paseo daemon restart makes `paseo send` fail for a few seconds with a coded error (2026-10-23, probed with
# `--json` against a closed port and an empty home). The plain-text error does NOT print the code, so the argv
# asks for --json, which writes {"error": {"code": ...}} to stderr. The four real codes are matched exactly,
# never as a substring of the output (the message text can echo anything): DAEMON_NOT_RUNNING is what a local
# home reports in the restart gap, DAEMON_UNREACHABLE a closed port, DAEMON_NOT_READY a daemon still starting,
# DAEMON_CONNECTION_LOST a daemon that went away mid-request.
SEND_TRANSIENT = ("DAEMON_UNREACHABLE", "DAEMON_CONNECTION_LOST", "DAEMON_NOT_READY", "DAEMON_NOT_RUNNING")
SEND_RETRIES = 2          # retries after the first attempt, paseo channel only
SEND_RETRY_PAUSE_S = 5.0
# send_to runs inside the 20 s launchd sample (launchd never overlaps a StartInterval job, so a long call only
# delays the next sample). A retry starts only while the whole call stays inside this budget; the first attempt
# keeps its old 60 s timeout, so the worst case is max(60 s, ~SEND_RETRY_BUDGET_S).
SEND_RETRY_BUDGET_S = 30.0
# One process-wide give-up (2026-10-23): set when a send ended on a SEND_TRANSIENT code with its retries spent
# or the budget out; the daemon is down for longer than a restart, so later send_to calls in this process make
# one attempt each instead of paying the retries again. Process memory only: every launchd sample is a new
# process, so the next sample retries afresh. A success clears it.
_paseo_down = False


def relay_env():
    """The environment for a relay.py call: relay refuses a sender it cannot resolve (exit 4, 2026-10-25), and this watcher runs
    from launchd with no session identity, so it declares one. A session identity still wins (relay reads RELAY_SENDER_NAME last)."""
    return {**os.environ, "RELAY_SENDER_NAME": os.environ.get("RELAY_SENDER_NAME") or "load-watch"}


def send_transient(r):
    """True when a failed `paseo send` reports one of the SEND_TRANSIENT codes: the exact `error.code` of the
    --json error on stderr (stdout is tried too). Anything else, including non-JSON output, is not transient."""
    for stream in (r.stderr, r.stdout):
        try:
            if json.loads(stream or "").get("error", {}).get("code") in SEND_TRANSIENT:
                return True
        except (ValueError, AttributeError, TypeError):
            continue
    return False


def send_to(w, text, defer=False):
    """One line into the watcher's session: `paseo send` for a Paseo agent (relay.py cannot reach one: no pane),
    else relay.py with --no-defer (an incident brief is time-critical: a busy watcher that cannot take it now is not
    reached, and the caller's fixer path runs). DEFER=True (only the `watcher test` registration check) lets relay.py
    queue it for a busy watcher. True only when the channel says it delivered it (or, DEFER, queued it). The paseo channel retries up to
    SEND_RETRIES times, SEND_RETRY_PAUSE_S apart and inside SEND_RETRY_BUDGET_S, but only when the failure's
    error code is exactly one of SEND_TRANSIENT (the daemon is restarting); relay.py gets one attempt. Once a
    send has given up on such a code, later calls in the same process make one attempt (`_paseo_down`).
    A retry after DAEMON_CONNECTION_LOST (or a retry killed by its timeout) can deliver the line twice, and a
    timed-out retry can leave `last_fail` stamped though the line arrived; the watcher investigates idempotently."""
    global _paseo_down
    if w["channel"] == "paseo":
        cli = w.get("paseo_cli") or "paseo"
        # PASEO_AGENT_ID unset so the daemon does not wrap it as agent-to-agent text; steer so a running turn
        # takes it without being torn down (bin/self-slash, 2026-10-20). `--` so text starting with `-` is
        # never read as an option.
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in ("PASEO_AGENT_ID", "PASEO_AGENT_CWD")}
        if w.get("paseo_home"):
            env["PASEO_HOME"] = w["paseo_home"]
        argv = [cli, "send", "--no-wait", "--json", "--behavior", "steer", "--", w["target"], text]
        retries = 0 if _paseo_down else SEND_RETRIES
    else:
        env, argv = relay_env(), [sys.executable, str(SF / "relay.py"), w["target"], text, *([] if defer else ["--no-defer"]), "--no-ack"]
        retries = 0
    started = time.monotonic()
    for attempt in range(retries + 1):
        try:
            left = 60 if attempt == 0 else min(60.0, SEND_RETRY_BUDGET_S - (time.monotonic() - started))
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=max(left, 1.0), env=env)
            if r.returncode == 0:
                if w["channel"] == "paseo":
                    _paseo_down = False
                return True
            transient = send_transient(r)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            return False
        if not transient:
            return False
        if attempt >= retries or time.monotonic() - started + SEND_RETRY_PAUSE_S >= SEND_RETRY_BUDGET_S:
            if w["channel"] == "paseo":
                _paseo_down = True
            return False
        time.sleep(SEND_RETRY_PAUSE_S)
    return False


def tell_watcher(text, dry, skip=()):
    """Tell the registered watcher, unless it is one of `skip` (the blamed session already got the brief).
    Returns True/False for sent or failed, None when there is no watcher or it was skipped."""
    w = watcher()
    if not w or w["target"] in skip or (w.get("sid") and w["sid"] in skip):
        return None
    if dry:
        print(f"watcher {w['channel']} {w['target']}: {text}")
        return None
    ok = send_to(w, f"load-watch, to the load watcher: {text} Investigate per the loadwatch skill.")
    w["last_ok" if ok else "last_fail"] = stamp()
    save_watcher(w)
    log(f"watcher {w['target']} told={ok}")
    return ok


def cmd_watcher(a):
    w = watcher()
    if a.op == "show":
        if not w:
            print("no load watcher registered", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        print(json.dumps(w, indent=1) if a.json else
              f"{w['channel']} {w['target']} ({w.get('name') or '-'}, cwd {w.get('cwd') or '-'}) since {w.get('since')}"
              + (f"; last told {w['last_ok']}" if w.get("last_ok") else "")
              + (f"; last failed {w['last_fail']}" if w.get("last_fail") else ""))
        return 0
    if a.op == "clear":
        if not w:
            print("no load watcher registered")
            return 0
        if a.target and a.target not in (w["target"], w.get("sid")):
            print(f"load-watch: the watcher is {w['target']}, not {a.target}; left it", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        (STATE_DIR / "watcher.json").unlink(missing_ok=True)
        print(f"cleared load watcher {w['target']}")
        return 0
    if a.op == "test":
        if not w:
            print("no load watcher registered", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        ok = send_to(w, a.target or "load-watch test: this session is the registered load watcher.", defer=True)
        print(f"{'sent to' if ok else 'could not reach'} {w['channel']} {w['target']}")
        return 0 if ok else 1
    # set: from flags, else this process's own session (a Paseo agent first: relay.py cannot reach one)
    paseo = a.paseo or (None if a.relay else os.environ.get("PASEO_AGENT_ID"))
    sid = a.sid or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")
    target = paseo or a.relay or sid or a.target
    if not target:
        print("load-watch watcher set: no session to register (pass --paseo ID or --relay TARGET)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    new = {"channel": "paseo" if paseo else "relay", "target": target, "sid": sid, "name": a.name,
           "cwd": a.cwd or os.getcwd(), "chain": a.chain, "since": stamp()}
    if paseo:
        new["paseo_cli"] = os.environ.get("PASEO_CLI") or "paseo"
        new["paseo_home"] = os.environ.get("PASEO_HOME")
    save_watcher(new)
    print(f"load watcher: {new['channel']} {target}")
    if w and w["target"] != target:
        print(f"replaced {w['channel']} {w['target']} ({w.get('name') or '-'}, since {w.get('since')})")
        told = send_to(w, f"load-watch: you are no longer the load watcher; {new['name'] or target} took over at "
                          f"{new['since']}. Stop any load-watch follow-up you were running; nothing else changes.")
        print(f"{'told' if told else 'could not reach'} the old watcher")
    return 0


# ---- job guard (djbclark, 2026-10-18) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# A frequent watchdog for launchd jobs: stop a job that hangs, eats resources, or crash-loops, cool it down,
# re-test it, and stop it for good after GUARD_MAX_ROUNDS rounds in a day. Why: that day three jobs had
# crash-looped ~6,000 times each since boot (landing on a Python upgrade, cua-driver "already running",
# signal-cli unlinked) and athena-lockers' aklog hung in uninterruptible AFS wait for 15+ minutes.
# Crash loops are checked for every job in the user's launchd domain; hangs and resources only for jobs
# listed in GUARD (label TAB key=value,... TAB note), because daemons such as litellm legitimately use CPU.
GUARD = Path(os.environ.get("LW_GUARD", HOME / ".config/load-watch/guard.tsv"))
GUARD_COOLDOWN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_GUARD_COOLDOWN_S", "5400"))  # 90 min, then a re-test
GUARD_TEST_S = 1800        # a re-enabled job that trips within this window starts the next round
GUARD_MAX_ROUNDS = 5       # rounds in 24 h before the job is disabled for good
LOOP_RUNS, LOOP_WINDOW_S = 20, 600   # crash loop: this many failed restarts within this window
# a slow crash loop (2026-10-20): litellm failed every ~32 s for 19 h after a half-finished upstream merge,
# ~19 restarts per 10 min, just under the fast rule, 2,169 restarts and never tripped
SLOW_LOOP_RUNS, SLOW_LOOP_WINDOW_S = 60, 7200
LOOP_CHECK_S = 120         # `launchctl print` failing jobs at most this often
LIMIT_KEYS = {"hang_s": 120.0, "max_cores": 0.0, "cores_s": 60.0, "max_rss_mb": 0.0, "max_runtime_s": 0.0}
GUARD_EXEMPT = {LABEL}


def guard_rows():
    rows = {}
    try:
        for ln in GUARD.read_text().splitlines():
            parts = ln.split("\t")
            if not parts[0] or parts[0].startswith("#"):
                continue
            lim = dict(LIMIT_KEYS)
            for kv in (parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else "").split(","):
                k, _, v = kv.partition("=")
                if k.strip() in lim:
                    try:
                        lim[k.strip()] = float(v)
                    except ValueError:
                        pass
            rows[parts[0]] = {"limits": lim, "note": parts[2] if len(parts) > 2 else ""}
    except OSError:
        pass
    return rows


def write_guard_rows(rows):
    GUARD.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = GUARD.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text("# launchd label\tlimits (hang_s, max_cores, cores_s, max_rss_mb, max_runtime_s; 0 = off)\tnote\n" +
                   "".join(f"{k}\t" + ",".join(f"{a}={b:g}" for a, b in v["limits"].items()) + f"\t{v['note']}\n"
                           for k, v in sorted(rows.items())))
    tmp.replace(GUARD)


def launchd_jobs():
    """label -> (pid or None, last exit status string), one `launchctl list`."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["launchctl", "list"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    jobs = {}
    for ln in out.splitlines()[1:]:
        p = ln.split("\t")
        if len(p) == 3:
            jobs[p[2]] = (int(p[0]) if p[0].isdigit() else None, p[1])
    return jobs


def job_info(label):
    """(runs, plist path) from `launchctl print`."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["launchctl", "print", f"gui/{MY_UID}/{label}"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                             timeout=20).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None, ""
    runs = re.search(r"^\s*runs = (\d+)", out, re.M)
    path = re.search(r"^\s*path = (\S.*)$", out, re.M)
    return (int(runs.group(1)) if runs else None), (path.group(1).strip() if path else "")


def tree(pid, table):
    kids = {}
    for p, row in table.items():
        kids.setdefault(str(row[0]), []).append(p)
    out, todo = [], [str(pid)]
    while todo:
        p = todo.pop()
        if p in table and p not in out:
            out.append(p)
            todo += kids.get(p, [])
    return out


def gevent(label, kind, detail):
    STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(STATE_DIR / "guard.jsonl", "a") as f:
        f.write(json.dumps({"t": stamp(), "label": label, "event": kind, "detail": detail}) + "\n")
    log(f"guard: {label}: {kind}: {detail}")


def gping(msg, dry):
    if not dry and HERMES_PING.exists():
        subprocess.run([str(HERMES_PING), f"djbclark-ade: load-watch guard: {msg}"], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
    tell_watcher(f"job guard: {msg}.", dry)


def guard_stop(label, reason, s, pids, table, t, dry):
    """Boot the job out, kill its processes, start a cooldown round (or stop it for good)."""
    if not s.get("plist"):
        s["plist"] = job_info(label)[1]
    rounds = [r for r in s.get("rounds", []) if t - r < 86400] + [t]
    final = len(rounds) >= GUARD_MAX_ROUNDS
    s.update(rounds=rounds, trip=reason, tripped=t, hot_since=None, u_since={}, run_since={})
    if final:
        s.update(state="permanent", until=None)
    else:
        s.update(state="cooldown", until=t + GUARD_COOLDOWN_S)
    if not dry:
        subprocess.run(["launchctl", "bootout", f"gui/{MY_UID}/{label}"], capture_output=True, timeout=30)
        if final:
            subprocess.run(["launchctl", "disable", f"gui/{MY_UID}/{label}"], capture_output=True, timeout=30)
        for sig in ("-TERM", "-KILL"):
            alive = [p for p in pids if p in table]
            if alive:
                subprocess.run(["kill", sig] + alive, capture_output=True, timeout=10)
                time.sleep(2)
    if final:
        gevent(label, "stopped-for-good", f"{reason}; round {len(rounds)} in 24 h")
        gping(f"stopped {label} for good after {len(rounds)} rounds today ({reason}); launchctl-disabled. "
              f"Bring it back: ~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/load-watch guard reset {label}", dry)
    else:
        back = time.strftime("%H:%M", time.localtime(s["until"]))
        gevent(label, "cooldown", f"{reason}; round {len(rounds)}/{GUARD_MAX_ROUNDS - 1} today, re-test at {back}")
        gping(f"stopped {label} ({reason}); cooldown round {len(rounds)} of {GUARD_MAX_ROUNDS - 1} allowed today, "
              f"re-test at {back}", dry)


def guard_restart(label, s, jobs, t, dry):
    """Cooldown over: load the job again and watch it for GUARD_TEST_S."""
    plist = s.get("plist", "")
    if label in jobs:  # someone loaded it meanwhile
        s.update(state="testing", until=t + GUARD_TEST_S)
        gevent(label, "re-test", "already loaded by someone else; watching it")
        return
    if not plist or not Path(plist).exists():
        s.update(state="released", until=None)
        gevent(label, "released", f"plist {plist or '?'} is gone; not restarting it")
        return
    if not dry:
        r = subprocess.run(["launchctl", "bootstrap", f"gui/{MY_UID}", plist], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=30)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            s.update(state="released", until=None)
            gevent(label, "released", f"bootstrap failed ({(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:120]}); left off")
            return
    s.update(state="testing", until=t + GUARD_TEST_S)
    gevent(label, "re-test", f"loaded again from {plist}; watching it for {GUARD_TEST_S / 60:g} min")


def guard(st, table, t, dry):
    g = st.setdefault("guard", {})
    jobs = launchd_jobs()
    if jobs is None:
        return
    rows = guard_rows()
    for label, s in list(g.items()):
        if s.get("state") == "cooldown" and t >= s.get("until", 0):
            guard_restart(label, s, jobs, t, dry)
        elif s.get("state") == "testing" and t >= s.get("until", 0):
            s.update(state="ok", until=None)
            gevent(label, "passed", f"no trip in {GUARD_TEST_S / 60:g} min after the re-test")
        elif s.get("state") in (None, "ok") and not s.get("rounds") and label not in rows and not s.get("loop"):
            g.pop(label)  # nothing to remember
    loop_check = t - st.get("guard_loop_t", 0) >= LOOP_CHECK_S
    if loop_check:
        st["guard_loop_t"] = t
    for label, (pid, status) in jobs.items():
        if label in GUARD_EXEMPT or label.startswith(("com.apple.", "application.")):
            continue  # never Apple's own agents, nor app instances launchd tracks for the GUI
        s = g.get(label) or {}
        if s.get("state") in ("cooldown", "permanent", "released"):
            continue
        reason, pids = None, (tree(pid, table) if pid else [])
        # a crash loop: a failing last exit and the restart count climbing
        if loop_check and status not in ("0", "-"):
            runs = job_info(label)[0]
            if runs is not None:
                hist = [h for h in s.get("loop", []) if t - h[0] <= SLOW_LOOP_WINDOW_S] + [[t, runs]]
                s["loop"] = hist
                fast = next(h for h in hist if t - h[0] <= LOOP_WINDOW_S)
                for base, need in ((fast, LOOP_RUNS), (hist[0], SLOW_LOOP_RUNS)):
                    if runs - base[1] >= need:
                        reason = (f"crash loop: {runs - base[1]} restarts in {(t - base[0]) / 60:.0f} min, "
                                  f"last exit {status}")
                        break
        elif status in ("0", "-"):
            s.pop("loop", None)
        lim = rows.get(label, {}).get("limits")
        if lim and pids and not reason:
            u = {p: s.get("u_since", {}).get(p, t) for p in pids if PSTATE.get(p, ("",))[0].startswith("U")}
            s["u_since"] = u
            stuck = [p for p, since in u.items() if lim["hang_s"] and t - since >= lim["hang_s"]]
            cores = sum(table[p][2] for p in pids)
            rss_mb = sum(PSTATE.get(p, ("", 0))[1] for p in pids) / 1024
            runs_for = t - s.get("run_since", {}).get(str(pid), t)
            s["run_since"] = {str(pid): s.get("run_since", {}).get(str(pid), t)}
            if lim["max_cores"] and cores > lim["max_cores"]:
                s["hot_since"] = s.get("hot_since") or t
            else:
                s["hot_since"] = None
            if stuck:
                reason = (f"hung: {table[stuck[0]][3][:70]} in uninterruptible wait "
                          f"{t - u[stuck[0]]:.0f} s")
            elif s.get("hot_since") and t - s["hot_since"] >= lim["cores_s"]:
                reason = f"{cores:.1f} cores for {t - s['hot_since']:.0f} s (limit {lim['max_cores']:g})"
            elif lim["max_rss_mb"] and rss_mb > lim["max_rss_mb"]:
                reason = f"{rss_mb:.0f} MB resident (limit {lim['max_rss_mb']:g})"
            elif lim["max_runtime_s"] and runs_for > lim["max_runtime_s"]:
                reason = f"running {runs_for / 60:.0f} min (limit {lim['max_runtime_s'] / 60:g})"
        elif lim and not pids:
            s.update(u_since={}, run_since={}, hot_since=None)
        if reason:
            guard_stop(label, reason, s, pids, table, t, dry)
        if s:
            g[label] = s


def cmd_guard(a):
    rows, st = guard_rows(), load_state()
    g = st.get("guard", {})
    if a.op == "status":
        for label, s in sorted(g.items()):
            when = time.strftime("%H:%M", time.localtime(s["until"])) if s.get("until") else "-"
            print(f"{label}\t{s.get('state', 'ok')}\tuntil {when}\trounds today "
                  f"{len([r for r in s.get('rounds', []) if now() - r < 86400])}\t{s.get('trip', '')}")
        return 0
    if a.op == "list":
        for k, v in sorted(rows.items()):
            print(f"{k}\t" + ",".join(f"{x}={y:g}" for x, y in v["limits"].items()) + f"\t{v['note']}")
        return 0
    if not a.label:
        print("load-watch guard add|rm|reset needs LABEL", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if a.op == "add":
        lim = dict(LIMIT_KEYS)
        for kv in a.limits:
            k, _, v = kv.partition("=")
            if k not in lim:
                print(f"load-watch guard add: unknown limit {k!r} (one of {', '.join(lim)})", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            lim[k] = float(v)
        rows[a.label] = {"limits": lim, "note": a.note or ""}
        write_guard_rows(rows)
    elif a.op == "rm":
        if rows.pop(a.label, None) is None:
            print(f"load-watch: {a.label} is not guarded", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        write_guard_rows(rows)
    elif a.op == "reset":  # bring a stopped job back now and forget its rounds
        s = g.pop(a.label, {})
        plist = s.get("plist") or job_info(a.label)[1]
        subprocess.run(["launchctl", "enable", f"gui/{MY_UID}/{a.label}"], capture_output=True, timeout=30)
        if plist and Path(plist).exists():
            subprocess.run(["launchctl", "bootstrap", f"gui/{MY_UID}", plist], capture_output=True, timeout=30)
        save_state(st)
        gevent(a.label, "reset", f"by hand; loaded from {plist or '?'}")
    print(f"{a.op} {a.label}")
    return 0


CHURN_SUSTAIN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_CHURN_SUSTAIN_S", "180"))  # seconds of churn above the admit limit
CHURN_EXCEPTION_RE = re.compile(r"Grok|Chrome|WindowServer")
_FAKE_COMPRESSOR_READS = [0]


def churn_counter():
    """Cumulative compressor pages (Compressions + Decompressions) now, or None when unreadable.
    LW_FAKE_COMPRESSOR (tests): a comma list of counters, one per call, the last repeating; set, vm_stat is not read."""
    raw = os.environ.get("LW_FAKE_COMPRESSOR", "").strip()
    if not raw:
        return _compressor_pages()
    vals = [float(x) for x in raw.split(",") if x.strip()]
    if not vals:
        return None
    i = min(_FAKE_COMPRESSOR_READS[0], len(vals) - 1)
    _FAKE_COMPRESSOR_READS[0] += 1
    return vals[i]


def churn_read(st, t):
    """One compressor-churn reading per sample: pages/s as the delta since the previous sample, or None (no
    reading: first sample, counter went backwards, a gap over MAX_GAP_S, no vm_stat). Keeps st['churn_since']
    while the churn is above ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S. State keys are read with .get, so an older state.json loads."""
    c = churn_counter()
    if c is None:  # no vm_stat: change nothing
        return None
    prev, prev_t = st.get("churn_prev"), st.get("churn_prev_t")
    st["churn_prev"], st["churn_prev_t"] = c, t
    ok = isinstance(prev, (int, float)) and isinstance(prev_t, (int, float))
    if not ok or not 0 < t - prev_t < MAX_GAP_S or c < prev:
        st["churn_since"] = None
        st.pop("churn_pages_s", None)
        return None
    rate = (c - prev) / (t - prev_t)
    st["churn_pages_s"] = round(rate)
    if rate <= ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S:
        st["churn_since"] = None
    elif not st.get("churn_since"):
        st["churn_since"] = t
    return rate


def sample_calm(st, t, churn, dry):
    """Feed the calm-boost hysteresis (calm.json) one 20 s reading, so a quiet half hour in which nobody called
    `admit` still counts. Calm = churn known and at most the boost line, free memory above the floor, pageins
    under their limit; a reading that cannot be taken is not calm. Pageins are a delta against the previous
    sample (st['pagein_prev'], .get so an older state.json loads). LW_FAKE_COMPRESSOR (tests) skips vm_stat."""
    calm = False
    if churn is not None and churn <= ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S:
        if os.environ.get("LW_FAKE_COMPRESSOR", "").strip():
            calm = True
        else:
            try:
                snap = vm_snapshot()
            except ReadFailed:
                snap = None  # a failed read is not calm
            if snap is not None:
                prev, prev_t = st.get("pagein_prev"), st.get("pagein_prev_t")
                st["pagein_prev"], st["pagein_prev_t"] = snap["pageins"], t
                if _num(prev) and _num(prev_t) and 0 < t - prev_t < MAX_GAP_S and snap["pageins"] >= prev:
                    calm = memory_calm(churn, snap["free_mb"], (snap["pageins"] - prev) / (t - prev_t))
    if not dry:
        calm_note(t, calm)


def churn_top(table, n=3):
    """The n commands using the most cores in this ps table, same-named ones summed: [(label, cores, matches the
    Grok/Chrome/WindowServer standing exception)]."""
    by = {}
    for _ppid, _uid, cores, cmd in table.values():
        if ".app/" in cmd:  # a bundle's executable name has spaces ("Google Chrome Helper (Renderer)")
            label = os.path.basename(cmd.split(" --")[0])
        else:
            label = " ".join(os.path.basename(w) for w in cmd.split()[:2])
        label = label[:40] or "?"
        row = by.setdefault(label, [0.0, False])
        row[0] += cores
        row[1] = row[1] or bool(CHURN_EXCEPTION_RE.search(cmd))
    return [(k, v[0], v[1]) for k, v in sorted(by.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][0])[:n] if v[0] > 0]


def churn_alert(st, t, table, dry):
    """Tell the watcher (hourly) and Hermes (every COOLDOWN_S) when churn has stayed above the admit limit for
    CHURN_SUSTAIN_S. Reads and warns only: no incident row, nothing is signalled or killed."""
    since = st.get("churn_since")
    if not since or t - since < CHURN_SUSTAIN_S:
        return
    cd = st["cooldown"]
    ping_due = "churn" not in cd
    last = cd.get("churn-watcher")
    watch_due = last is None or t - last >= WATCHER_NOCPU_S
    if not (ping_due or watch_due):
        return
    top = churn_top(table)
    body = (f"compressor churn ~{st.get('churn_pages_s', 0) / 1000:.0f}k pages/s for {CHURN_SUSTAIN_S / 60:g}+ min "
            f"(limit {ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S / 1000:g}k); top: "
            + (", ".join(f"{label} {cores:.1f} cores" for label, cores, _ in top) or "none") + ". "
            "Admit already holds new bg/acp-dispatch work; this is running or bypass work.")
    tail = "do not kill or SIGSTOP without djbclark."
    if any(exc for _l, _c, exc in top):  # advice shape only: the alert is never suppressed
        tail += (" Standing exception: Grok Bot/Chrome renderers routinely use 0.3-0.7 cores each, so do not ask "
                 "djbclark to quit or reload them for routine load; only if far above that or agents time out.")
    full = f"load-watch: {body} Investigate per the loadwatch skill; {tail}"
    if dry:
        print(full)
        tell_watcher(f"{body} {tail[0].upper() + tail[1:]}", True)
        return
    log(f"compressor churn {st.get('churn_pages_s', 0)} pages/s since {stamp(since)}; top: {body.split('top: ')[1]}")
    if ping_due:
        if HERMES_PING.exists():
            try:
                subprocess.run([str(HERMES_PING), f"djbclark-ade: {full}"], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
            except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
                log(f"churn ping failed: {e!r}")
        cd["churn"] = t
    if watch_due and tell_watcher(f"{body} {tail[0].upper() + tail[1:]}", False) is not None:
        cd["churn-watcher"] = t


CHROME_CORES = float(os.environ.get("LW_CHROME_CORES", "0.9"))
CHROME_SUSTAIN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_CHROME_SUSTAIN_S", "300"))
CHROME_RE = re.compile(r"/Google Chrome\.app/Contents/")  # not "Google Chrome for Testing" (an agent's puppeteer)


def chrome_kind(cmd):
    m = re.search(r"--type=(\S+)", cmd)
    return {"renderer": "tab renderer", "gpu-process": "GPU process"}.get(m.group(1), m.group(1)) if m else "browser (main) process"


def chrome_alert(st, t, table, dry):
    """Tell the watcher (hourly per process) when one Chrome process has used CHROME_CORES or more for
    CHROME_SUSTAIN_S (2026-10-25: the main process sat at 97% for 11 min on one page). Warns only: no incident,
    nothing is signalled or killed; the advice is the Task Manager (Shift+Esc), a human step."""
    hot = {pid: (c, cmd) for pid, (_pp, _uid, c, cmd) in table.items() if c >= CHROME_CORES and CHROME_RE.search(cmd)}
    since = {k: v for k, v in st.get("chrome_hot", {}).items() if k in {str(p) for p in hot}}  # str pids (json)
    for pid in hot:
        since.setdefault(str(pid), t)
    st["chrome_hot"] = since
    cd = st["cooldown"]
    for pid, (cores, cmd) in hot.items():
        key = f"chrome:{pid}"
        if t - since[str(pid)] < CHROME_SUSTAIN_S or key in cd and t - cd[key] < WATCHER_NOCPU_S:
            continue
        url = re.search(r"(https?://\S+)", cmd)
        kind = chrome_kind(cmd)
        if kind == "tab renderer":
            advice = (f"sort by CPU and match pid {pid} to its task. Only if the task is an identified tab and "
                      "djbclark chooses, End process on that tab, then reload it.")
        else:
            advice = (f"sort by CPU and match pid {pid} to its task. Report the task name and CPU percentage; "
                      f"a {kind} alert does not identify a busy tab. Do not end tabs based on this alert alone.")
        body = (f"Chrome {kind} pid {pid} has used ~{cores:.1f} cores for {(t - since[str(pid)]) / 60:.0f}+ min"
                + (f" (opened {url.group(1)[:80]})" if url else "") + ". Tell djbclark: Chrome Task Manager (Shift+Esc), "
                + advice + " Do not kill, reload, or restart Chrome yourself.")
        if dry:
            print(f"load-watch: {body}")
            continue
        if tell_watcher(body, False) is not None:
            cd[key] = t
            log(body)


MDS_CORES = float(os.environ.get("LW_MDS_CORES", "0.5"))
MDS_SUSTAIN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_MDS_SUSTAIN_S", "120"))
MDS_MAX_GAP_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_MDS_MAX_GAP_S", "90"))  # samples run every ~20 s; longer is a sleep or a stall
MDS_COOLDOWN_S = float(os.environ.get("LW_MDS_COOLDOWN_S", "1800"))
MDS_HELPER = "/usr/local/libexec/djbclark/mds-xpc-clients"  # root:wheel 0755, one NOPASSWD sudoers line, no arguments
MDS_PEER_RE = re.compile(r"(\d+) (\d+) ([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 ._+-]*)")


def mds_peers():
    """Processes holding a send right to mds as ["COUNT PID NAME", ...], busiest first (at most 6), or None when the
    root helper is missing, sudo refuses (it never prompts: -n), it fails or takes over 20 s. Only lines of the
    exact helper shape are kept; nothing is passed to the helper and nothing from it reaches a shell."""
    if not os.path.exists(MDS_HELPER):
        return None
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["sudo", "-n", MDS_HELPER], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    return [ln for ln in r.stdout.splitlines() if MDS_PEER_RE.fullmatch(ln)][:6]


def exe_name(cmd):
    """Basename of the program (first token) only, restricted to [A-Za-z0-9._+-]. Never an argument: those can
    hold secrets (`env TOKEN=x cmd`, `mysql -pSECRET`) and a path argument must not make a process look like another."""
    tok = cmd.split(None, 1)[0] if cmd.strip() else ""
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._+-]", "", os.path.basename(tok))


def mds_probe(st, t, table, dry):
    """Record who is busy while Spotlight's mds is (2026-11-01: mds sat at 25-70% for hours; the cause was Finder
    re-listing /private/tmp, found only by hand with `sample` and `fs_usage`, both root). Needs no root: once mds
    has used MDS_CORES or more over consecutive samples spanning MDS_SUSTAIN_S (a gap over MDS_MAX_GAP_S restarts
    the span), log one line per MDS_COOLDOWN_S with mds, Finder and the six busiest other processes by program
    name only. A log line only: it pings nobody and signals nothing. XPC client pids (`lsmp`) need root:
    macos/mds-xpc-clients in site-public-djbclark is the root helper, a later change calls it."""
    mds = sum(c for _pp, uid, c, cmd in table.values() if uid == 0 and exe_name(cmd) == "mds")  # root's, not a lookalike
    last, st["mds_last"] = st.get("mds_last"), t
    if mds < MDS_CORES or (last is not None and t - last > MDS_MAX_GAP_S):
        st.pop("mds_hot", None)
        if mds < MDS_CORES:
            return
    since = st.setdefault("mds_hot", t)
    cd = st["cooldown"]
    if t - since < MDS_SUSTAIN_S or t - cd.get("mds", -MDS_COOLDOWN_S) < MDS_COOLDOWN_S:
        return
    finder = sum(c for _pp, _uid, c, cmd in table.values() if exe_name(cmd) == "Finder")
    others = sorted(((c, pid, exe_name(cmd)) for pid, (_pp, uid, c, cmd) in table.items() if not (uid == 0 and exe_name(cmd) == "mds")),
                    reverse=True)[:6]
    top = "; ".join(f"{pid} {c:.2f} {name}" for c, pid, name in others)
    line = f"mds probe: mds {mds:.2f} cores for {(t - since) / 60:.0f}+ min, Finder {finder:.2f}; top others: {top}"
    if dry:
        print(f"load-watch: {line}")
        return
    peers = mds_peers()  # root helper; None keeps the line as it was
    if peers:
        line += "; xpc clients (ports pid name): " + "; ".join(peers)
    log(line)
    cd["mds"] = t

def prune_cooldowns(cd, t):
    """Drop cooldown stamps older than their hold: COOLDOWN_S, or longer for a key whose own hold is longer
    (the mds probe's LW_MDS_COOLDOWN_S can exceed LW_COOLDOWN_H; pruned early it would log again at once)."""
    own = {"mds": MDS_COOLDOWN_S}
    return {k: v for k, v in cd.items() if t - v < max(COOLDOWN_S, own.get(k, 0))}

def cmd_sample(a):
    st = load_state()
    t = now()
    load1 = os.getloadavg()[0]
    ncpu = os.cpu_count() or 1
    hot = load1 / ncpu >= LOAD_PER_CORE
    gap = t - st.get("t", 0)
    st["t"] = t
    try:  # a churn problem must never stop load sampling
        sample_calm(st, t, churn_read(st, t), a.dry_run)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        log(f"churn read error: {e!r}")
    # Time, not a sample count (2026-10-18: under a load-60 stall launchd ran us every 3-7 minutes, so 15
    # samples took 45+ min and one 7-min gap restarted the count). A gap over MAX_GAP_S is a sleep.
    if hot and (not st.get("hot_since") or gap >= MAX_GAP_S):
        st["hot_since"], st["samples"], st["streak"] = t, [], 0
    elif not hot:
        st["hot_since"], st["samples"], st["streak"] = None, [], 0
    table = ps_table()
    if table is None:  # a stall this bad is itself a hot sample: keep the streak going, add no CPU data
        log(f"ps timed out at load {load1:.0f}; sample counted, no CPU data")
        st["streak"] = st.get("streak", 0) + hot
        save_state(st)
        return 0
    try:
        guard(st, table, t, a.dry_run)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - the guard must never stop load sampling
        log(f"guard error: {e!r}")
    if hot:
        d = {pid: [round(c, 2), uid, cmd[:300], ppid] for pid, (ppid, uid, c, cmd) in table.items() if c >= 0.05}
        st["samples"] = [x for x in st.get("samples", []) if x["t"] >= t - SUSTAIN_S] + [{"t": t, "d": d}]
        st["streak"] = st.get("streak", 0) + 1
    st["load1"] = load1
    st["cooldown"] = prune_cooldowns(st.get("cooldown", {}), t)
    try:
        churn_alert(st, t, table, a.dry_run)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        log(f"churn alert error: {e!r}")
    try:
        chrome_alert(st, t, table, a.dry_run)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        log(f"chrome alert error: {e!r}")
    try:
        mds_probe(st, t, table, a.dry_run)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        log(f"mds probe error: {e!r}")
    if a.verbose:
        print(f"load {load1:.1f}/{ncpu} hot={hot} streak={st['streak']}")
    if hot and t - st["hot_since"] >= SUSTAIN_S:
        use, span = window(st)
        parent = ppids(st, table)
        groups, loose = attribute(use, span, parent)
        told = 0
        for g in sorted(groups.values(), key=lambda g: -g["cores"]):
            s = g["session"]
            if g["cores"] < MIN_CORES or not g["procs"]:
                continue
            sid_key = f"sid:{s.get('sid') or s['id']}"
            if sid_key in st["cooldown"] or t - st["cooldown"].get("skip:" + sid_key, 0) < 600:
                continue
            # the repo is the work's, not the session's cwd (2026-10-18): lsof and git, so only for a session
            # about to be told, never per sample
            work = work_repos(g, git_top(s["cwd"]) if s.get("cwd") else "", parent, proc_cmds(st, table))
            top = work["repos"][0]["top"] if work["repos"] else ""
            repo_keys = [f"repo:{r['top']}" for r in work["repos"]]
            if repo_keys and all(k in st["cooldown"] for k in repo_keys):
                st["cooldown"]["skip:" + sid_key] = t  # do not redo the lsof every 20 s sample
                continue
            keys = [sid_key] + repo_keys
            inc = time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M", time.localtime(t)) + f"-{s['id'][:8]}"
            path = STATE_DIR / "briefs" / f"{inc}.md"
            if not a.dry_run:
                path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                path.write_text(brief(inc, g, work, load1, ncpu))
            relayed, ping = notify(inc, g, top, path, load1, ncpu, a.dry_run)
            watched = tell_watcher(ping.removeprefix("djbclark-ade: ") + ".", a.dry_run,
                                   skip=({s.get("sid"), s["id"]} - {None}) if relayed else ())
            rec = {"id": inc, "t": stamp(t), "load1": round(load1, 1), "ncpu": ncpu, "cores": round(g["cores"], 2),
                   "agent": s.get("agent"), "session": s.get("name") or s["id"], "sid": s.get("sid"),
                   "cwd": s.get("cwd"), "repo": top, "repo_guess": work["guess"],
                   "repos": [{k: r[k] for k in ("top", "cores", "bg_cores", "rule")} for r in work["repos"]],
                   "procs": g["procs"][:8], "relayed": relayed, "watcher_told": watched,
                   "brief": str(path), "dry_run": a.dry_run}
            if a.dry_run:
                print(json.dumps(rec, indent=1))
                print(ping)
                continue
            for k in keys:
                st["cooldown"][k] = t
            with open(STATE_DIR / "incidents.jsonl", "a") as f:
                f.write(json.dumps(rec) + "\n")
            log(f"incident {inc} {rec['session']} {rec['cores']} cores relayed={relayed}")
            told += 1
        if a.verbose or a.dry_run:
            for row in loose[:5]:
                print(f"unattributed: pid {row['pid']} {row['cores']} cores {row['cmd'][:100]}")
        if not told and not st.get("loose_logged"):
            why = not_cpu(use, span, ncpu)
            log("sustained load, no agent session above threshold; " + why + "; top: " +
                "; ".join(f"{r['cores']} {r['cmd'][:60]}" for r in loose[:3]))
            st["loose_logged"] = True
            # 2026-10-18: load 90 from memory starvation and a hung AFS aklog blamed no agent and told no one
            msg = f"load {load1:.0f} on {ncpu} cores for {SUSTAIN_S / 60:g}+ min and no agent build behind it; {why}"
            if "nocpu" not in st["cooldown"] and not a.dry_run:
                if HERMES_PING.exists():
                    subprocess.run([str(HERMES_PING), f"djbclark-ade: load-watch: {msg}"], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
                st["cooldown"]["nocpu"] = t
            # the watcher hears a recurrence hourly, Hermes only every COOLDOWN_S (djbclark, 2026-10-20)
            last = st["cooldown"].get("nocpu-watcher")
            if not a.dry_run and (last is None or t - last >= WATCHER_NOCPU_S):
                if tell_watcher(msg + ".", a.dry_run) is not None:
                    st["cooldown"]["nocpu-watcher"] = t
    elif not hot:
        st.pop("loose_logged", None)
    save_state(st)
    return 0


def not_cpu(use, span, ncpu):
    """One line on what the load is when no session's CPU explains it: sampled CPU, swap, stuck processes."""
    cpu = sum(r[0] for r in use.values()) / span if span else 0
    try:
        swap = subprocess.run(["sysctl", "-n", "vm.swapusage"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5).stdout
        swap = " ".join(swap.split()[:6]).replace(" = ", "=")
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        swap = "?"
    stuck = sorted(set(STUCK))
    counts = {}
    for c in BGRUN:
        counts[c] = counts.get(c, 0) + 1
    top = sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1])[:4]
    return (f"processes used ~{cpu:.1f} of {ncpu} cores; swap {swap}; "
            f"{len(stuck)} stuck in disk/network wait" + (f": {', '.join(stuck[:4])}" if stuck else "") +
            f"; {len(BGRUN)} runnable at background priority" +
            (": " + ", ".join(f"{n}x {c}" for c, n in top) if top else ""))


def cmd_status(a):
    st = load_state()
    use, span = window(st)
    print(f"load1 {st.get('load1', 0):.1f} on {os.cpu_count()} cores; hot for {now() - st['hot_since'] if st.get('hot_since') else 0:.0f}/{SUSTAIN_S:.0f} s, {st.get('streak', 0)} samples "
          f"(threshold {LOAD_PER_CORE}/core, {MIN_CORES} cores per session, cooldown {COOLDOWN_S / 3600:g} h)")
    for pid, (secs, _, cmd) in sorted(use.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][0])[:8]:
        print(f"  {secs / span if span else 0:5.2f} cores  pid {pid}  {cmd[:110]}")
    if st.get("churn_pages_s") is not None:
        print(f"  compressor churn {st['churn_pages_s'] / 1000:.0f}k pages/s (admit limit {ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S / 1000:g}k)"
              + (f", above it for {now() - st['churn_since']:.0f}/{CHURN_SUSTAIN_S:.0f} s" if st.get("churn_since") else ""))
    cs = calm_load().get("calm_since")
    if _num(cs):
        print(f"  calm boost: calm for {now() - cs:.0f}/{ADMIT_BOOST_CALM_S:g} s (the {ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE:g}/core boost applies after that; any hot reading resets it)")
    for k, v in st.get("cooldown", {}).items():
        print(f"  cooldown {k} until {stamp(v + {'nocpu-watcher': WATCHER_NOCPU_S, 'churn-watcher': WATCHER_NOCPU_S, 'mds': MDS_COOLDOWN_S}.get(k, COOLDOWN_S))}")
    return 0


def incidents():
    try:
        return [json.loads(ln) for ln in (STATE_DIR / "incidents.jsonl").read_text().splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    except OSError:
        return []


def cmd_incidents(a):
    for r in incidents()[-a.n:]:
        ack = f"  ack: {r['ack']}" if r.get("ack") else ""
        print(f"{r['id']}  {r['t']}  load {r['load1']}  {r['agent']} {r['session']}  {r['cores']} cores  "
              f"{r.get('repo') or r.get('cwd')}  relayed={r['relayed']}{ack}")
    return 0


def cmd_ack(a):
    rows = incidents()
    hit = next((r for r in rows if r["id"] == a.id), None)
    if not hit:
        print(f"load-watch: no incident {a.id}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    hit["ack"] = f"{stamp()} {a.note}"
    tmp = STATE_DIR / "incidents.jsonl.tmp"
    tmp.write_text("".join(json.dumps(r) + "\n" for r in rows))
    tmp.replace(STATE_DIR / "incidents.jsonl")
    print(f"recorded ack for {a.id}")
    return 0


def cmd_ci(a):
    rows = registry()
    if a.op == "list":
        for k, v in sorted(rows.items()):
            print("\t".join([k] + v))
        return 0
    if not a.dir:
        print("load-watch ci check|rm|decide needs DIR", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    top = a.dir.rstrip("/") if a.dir.endswith("/*") else (git_top(a.dir) or os.path.realpath(a.dir))
    if a.op == "check":  # bg: "mode<TAB>text<TAB>key", exit 1 when undecided
        key, row = decision(top, rows)
        if row is None:
            return 1
        print(f"{row[0]}\t{row[1]}\t{key}")
        return 0
    if a.op == "decide":
        if a.mode not in MODES or not a.text:
            print('load-watch ci decide DIR ci "CI command"|local "why"|pending "note"', file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        rows[top] = [a.mode, a.text, time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")]
    elif a.op == "rm":
        if rows.pop(top, None) is None:
            print(f"load-watch: {top} has no decision", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    write_registry(rows)
    print(f"{a.op} {top}" + (f" {a.mode}" if a.op == "decide" else ""))
    return 0


def cmd_ci_only(a):
    rows = registry()
    if a.op == "list":
        for k, v in sorted(rows.items()):
            if v[0] == "ci":
                print(f"{k}\t{v[1]}\t{v[2]}")
        return 0
    if not a.dir:
        print("load-watch ci-only add|rm|check needs DIR", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    top = git_top(a.dir) or os.path.realpath(a.dir)
    if a.op == "check":
        if rows.get(top, [""])[0] == "ci":
            print(rows[top][1])
            return 0
        return 1
    if a.op == "add":
        if not a.ci_cmd:
            print("load-watch ci-only add DIR \"CI command\"", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        rows[top] = ["ci", a.ci_cmd, time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")]
    elif a.op == "rm":
        if rows.pop(top, None) is None:
            print(f"load-watch: {top} is not registered", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    write_registry(rows)
    print(f"{a.op} {top}")
    return 0


ADMIT_PER_CORE = 1.5  # admit's own default base; `bg` passes its own (2.5 since 2026-11-01). LOAD_PER_CORE (4.0) is only the blame step
ADMIT_FRESH_S = 120   # state.json older than this says nothing about the machine now


def _env_float(name, default, lo=0.0):
    """A finite number >= lo from the environment, else `default` (a typo must not crash the launchd sampler)."""
    try:
        v = float(os.environ.get(name, "").strip() or default)
    except ValueError:
        return default
    return v if math.isfinite(v) and v >= lo else default


# Memory gate (operator 2026-10-23): load alone cannot tell a busy host from a thrashing one (the 2026-10-23
# spike was load 42-74 with kern.memorystatus_level 37% and swap 86-92%, the same swap a calm hour shows).
# What it did show was compressor churn. Calibrated 2026-10-23 from 215 ten-second samples (10:20-10:52):
# load<10 p50 34k, 10-25 p50 49k, >=25 p50 80k and p90 108k pages/s; the calm tail read 11-22k. The limit was 60000.
# 2026-11-01 (load watcher d8891c91, measured): a sustained load of 35-70 on this 8-core, 16 GB Mac was memory
# starvation, not CPU: ~64 MB free, ~12k compressions+decompressions/s, ~1760 pageins/s, kernel_task 57% and sys
# 25-39% of the CPU, 31+ live agent processes (omp 20, copilot 11, claude 8, agy 3). The 4.0 calm boost let a slice
# start in every brief dip and each start pushed memory back over: an oscillation. So admit now fails toward
# WAITING: a free-memory floor, a lower compressor limit (12k/s was already starving, 20000 is the line), a pageins
# limit and a cap on live `acp-run` sessions, all env-tunable; a reading that cannot be taken is said so, never guessed.
ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S = _env_float("LW_MAX_COMPRESSOR_S", 20000.0, 1.0)
ADMIT_MIN_FREE_MB = _env_float("LW_MIN_FREE_MB", 600.0)
ADMIT_PAGEINS_S = _env_float("LW_MAX_PAGEINS_S", 1000.0, 1.0)
ADMIT_MAX_AGENTS = int(_env_float("LW_MAX_AGENTS", 14, 0))  # 0 = no cap
ADMIT_MEM_WINDOW_S = 2.0  # vm_stat is read twice this far apart; the counters' deltas are the per-second rates
# Calm boost (operator 2026-10-25, "make the change" after a load of 12-14 with no UI lag): while the compressor is
# calm the per-core limit rises from ADMIT_PER_CORE to ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE. The signal is churn, not swap: swap sat
# at 86-92% in calm hours too (above), so a swap condition would almost never boost. A churn that cannot be read
# (no vm_stat) never boosts.
# 2026-11-01 (operator): the boost limit rose from 2.0 to 4.0 per core. A load of 3.5 per core "is actually not too bad for
# this system"; the real constraint on this 16 GB, 8-core Mac is memory pressure (compressor churn, swap) and process churn
# (2026-10-31: five parallel pytest runs forked thousands of short git processes, load 222, swap 7.9/9.2 GB).
# Same day, hysteresis: the boost applies only after the machine has been calm (churn at most the boost line, free
# memory above the floor, pageins under their limit) for LW_BOOST_CALM_S (600) seconds without a break; any hot
# reading, by `admit` or by the 20 s sampler, resets the clock (calm.json in the state dir). The boost line now
# equals the compressor limit: churn between 20k and 25k used to boost and is now refused outright.
ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE = 4.0
ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S = ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S
ADMIT_BOOST_CALM_S = _env_float("LW_BOOST_CALM_S", 600.0)
# Agent reservations (Codex review of PR 210, 2026-11-01): two dispatchers that both read 13 of 14 live agents and
# spend 2 s sampling memory would both be admitted before either launches. An admission under the cap is therefore
# recorded (agent-reservations.json under an flock, `{"r": [{"id", "until"}]}`) and counted with the live acp-run
# processes until it is released or expires. acp-dispatch releases it (`load-watch release ID`) the moment its agent
# is spawned (the live count takes over; the entry then lives RELEASE_GRACE_S more, covering the seconds before
# acp-run shows in ps) or the launch is refused; the expiry, LW_RESERVE_S (default 1200: it must outlast the
# dispatcher's own pre-spawn capacity wait of up to 900 s), is only the backstop for a dispatcher that died.
# LW_RESERVE_S=0 turns reservations off; `--no-reserve` makes one call a pure check.
ADMIT_RESERVE_S = _env_float("LW_RESERVE_S", 1200.0)
RELEASE_GRACE_S = 30.0
CALM_GAP_S = ADMIT_FRESH_S  # calm.json's last reading older than this: nobody watched in between, the clock restarts
EX_TEMPFAIL = 75


def _fake_list(name):
    raw = os.environ.get(name, "").strip()
    return [float(x) for x in raw.split(",") if x.strip()] if raw else []


def _fake_loads():
    """LW_FAKE_LOAD1 (tests): one load, or a comma list read one per poll with the last value repeating."""
    return _fake_list("LW_FAKE_LOAD1")


def _fake_churn():
    """LW_FAKE_CHURN (tests): pages/s, or a comma list read one per poll with the last value repeating."""
    return _fake_list("LW_FAKE_CHURN")


def _fake_memory():
    """LW_FAKE_FREE_MB, LW_FAKE_PAGEINS, LW_FAKE_AGENTS (tests): each a number or a comma list, one per poll, last repeating."""
    return {k: _fake_list(env) for k, env in (("free_mb", "LW_FAKE_FREE_MB"), ("pageins_s", "LW_FAKE_PAGEINS"),
                                              ("agents", "LW_FAKE_AGENTS"))}


class ReadFailed(Exception):
    """A reading source that EXISTS on this host (vm_stat, /proc, ps) failed: timed out, exited non-zero or printed
    something unparsable. That is likeliest exactly when the machine is starving (a fork+exec stalls), so `admit`
    treats it as hot (refuses), never as open. A source that is absent altogether returns None instead."""


def _vm_stat_snapshot():
    """{free_mb, compress, pageins} from macOS `vm_stat` (free = Pages free + Pages speculative; compress =
    Compressions + Decompressions, cumulative pages). None when there is no `vm_stat` binary; ReadFailed when it
    exists and fails."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["vm_stat"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        raise ReadFailed(f"vm_stat: {e!r}") from e
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise ReadFailed(f"vm_stat exited {r.returncode}")
    out = r.stdout
    v = {m.group(1): int(m.group(2)) for m in
         re.finditer(r"^(Pages free|Pages speculative|Pageins|Compressions|Decompressions):\s+(\d+)", out, re.M)}
    ps = re.search(r"page size of (\d+) bytes", out)
    try:
        page = int(ps.group(1)) if ps else (os.sysconf("SC_PAGE_SIZE") or 16384)
    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:
        raise ReadFailed(f"vm_stat page size: {e!r}") from e
    if not all(k in v for k in ("Pages free", "Pageins", "Compressions", "Decompressions")):
        raise ReadFailed("vm_stat output lacks a needed counter")
    return {"free_mb": (v["Pages free"] + v.get("Pages speculative", 0)) * page / 1048576,
            "compress": v["Compressions"] + v["Decompressions"], "pageins": v["Pageins"]}


def _proc_snapshot():
    """The Linux equivalents (2026-11-01, uncalibrated: swap pages/s against a line set for the macOS compressor, so
    that gate rarely trips there; pgmajfault counts faults): free = MemAvailable (else MemFree) in /proc/meminfo,
    compress = pswpin + pswpout and pageins = pgmajfault in /proc/vmstat. None when /proc/meminfo does not exist;
    ReadFailed when it exists and cannot be read or parsed."""
    try:
        meminfo = Path("/proc/meminfo").read_text()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise ReadFailed(f"/proc/meminfo: {e!r}") from e
    try:
        mem = {m.group(1): int(m.group(2)) for m in re.finditer(r"^(MemAvailable|MemFree):\s+(\d+) kB", meminfo, re.M)}
        vm = {m.group(1): int(m.group(2)) for m in re.finditer(r"^(pswpin|pswpout|pgmajfault) (\d+)",
                                                               Path("/proc/vmstat").read_text(), re.M)}
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise ReadFailed(f"/proc/vmstat: {e!r}") from e
    free_kb = mem.get("MemAvailable", mem.get("MemFree"))
    if free_kb is None or not all(k in vm for k in ("pswpin", "pswpout", "pgmajfault")):
        raise ReadFailed("/proc counters missing")
    return {"free_mb": free_kb / 1024, "compress": vm["pswpin"] + vm["pswpout"], "pageins": vm["pgmajfault"]}


def vm_snapshot():
    """One memory snapshot, or None when this host has neither vm_stat nor /proc/meminfo; ReadFailed when the
    source it has fails."""
    s = _vm_stat_snapshot()
    return s if s is not None else _proc_snapshot()


def _compressor_pages():
    """Compressions + Decompressions (cumulative) for the sampler, or None where unreadable (it never refuses)."""
    try:
        s = vm_snapshot()
    except ReadFailed:
        return None
    return s["compress"] if s else None


def is_acp_run(argv):
    """True for the process that IS an acp-run session: argv[0] or the script right after a python interpreter
    (any case: a framework `Python`; `-X opt` and `-W opt` skipped) is named exactly `acp-run`. `uv run --script
    .../acp-run` (argv[0] `uv`, whose python child is the session), `python -c`/`-m` and anything that merely
    mentions acp-run in an argument do not match, so each session counts once."""
    if not argv:
        return False
    if os.path.basename(argv[0]) == "acp-run":
        return True
    if not re.fullmatch(r"python[\d.]*", os.path.basename(argv[0]), re.I):
        return False
    args, i = argv[1:], 0
    while i < len(args):
        x = args[i]
        if x in ("-X", "-W"):
            i += 2
        elif x in ("-c", "-m"):
            return False
        elif x.startswith("-"):
            i += 1
        else:
            return os.path.basename(x) == "acp-run"
    return False


def count_agents():
    """Live acp-run sessions machine-wide, from one `ps` (exact argv match, never pgrep/pkill -f). None when there
    is no `ps` binary; ReadFailed when ps times out, exits non-zero or prints a table without this process in it."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["ps", "-axo", "pid=,args="], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        raise ReadFailed(f"ps: {e!r}") from e
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise ReadFailed(f"ps exited {r.returncode}")
    rows = [ln.split(None, 1) for ln in r.stdout.splitlines()]
    rows = [p for p in rows if len(p) == 2 and p[0].isdigit()]
    if str(os.getpid()) not in {p[0] for p in rows}:   # an empty or malformed table (this very process must be in it)
        raise ReadFailed("ps printed no usable process table")
    return sum(1 for p in rows if is_acp_run(p[1].split()))


def admit_memory(fake_load, fake_churn, fake_mem, polls, max_agents=0):
    """One memory reading: {churn, free_mb, pageins_s, agents}, each None when it cannot be read (said so in the
    record, never guessed). Real mode reads vm_stat twice ADMIT_MEM_WINDOW_S apart. Test hooks: tests that fake the
    load (or any reading) get a healthy default for the readings they do not fake, so a busy host cannot change
    their answer."""
    def pick(vals, default):
        return vals[min(polls, len(vals) - 1)] if vals else default

    if fake_load or fake_churn or any(fake_mem.values()):
        return {"churn": pick(fake_churn, 0.0), "free_mb": pick(fake_mem["free_mb"], 8192.0),
                "pageins_s": pick(fake_mem["pageins_s"], 0.0), "agents": int(pick(fake_mem["agents"], 0)), "failed": set()}
    m = {"churn": None, "free_mb": None, "pageins_s": None, "agents": None, "failed": set()}
    if max_agents:  # the cap gates only callers that START agents (acp-dispatch); everyone else skips the ps
        try:
            m["agents"] = count_agents()
        except ReadFailed:
            m["failed"].add("agents")
    try:
        a = vm_snapshot()
        if a is not None:
            t0 = time.monotonic()
            time.sleep(ADMIT_MEM_WINDOW_S)
            b = vm_snapshot()
            if b is None:
                raise ReadFailed("second vm sample missing")
            dt = time.monotonic() - t0
            dt = dt if dt > 0 else ADMIT_MEM_WINDOW_S
            m.update(churn=max(0.0, (b["compress"] - a["compress"]) / dt), free_mb=b["free_mb"],
                     pageins_s=max(0.0, (b["pageins"] - a["pageins"]) / dt))
    except ReadFailed:
        m["failed"].add("memory")
    return m


def admit_reading(fake, polls):
    """(load1, cores, per_core) now; `fake` is _fake_loads() and `polls` how many reads came before."""
    load1 = fake[min(polls, len(fake) - 1)] if fake else os.getloadavg()[0]
    cores = os.cpu_count() or 1
    return load1, cores, load1 / cores


def admit_limit(base, churn, boost=ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE, boost_churn=ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S):
    """The per-core limit in force: `boost` (when above `base`) while the compressor churn is known and at most
    `boost_churn`, else `base`. boost None or 0 disables it."""
    if boost and boost > base and churn is not None and churn <= boost_churn:
        return boost
    return base


def memory_calm(churn, free_mb, pageins_s, boost_churn=None, min_free=None, max_pageins=None):
    """True when every memory reading is known and under its line (a reading that is None is never calm)."""
    boost_churn = ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S if boost_churn is None else boost_churn
    min_free = ADMIT_MIN_FREE_MB if min_free is None else min_free
    max_pageins = ADMIT_PAGEINS_S if max_pageins is None else max_pageins
    return (churn is not None and free_mb is not None and pageins_s is not None
            and churn <= boost_churn and free_mb >= min_free and pageins_s <= max_pageins)


def calm_load():
    try:
        s = json.loads((STATE_DIR / "calm.json").read_text())
        return s if isinstance(s, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def calm_note(t, calm):
    """Record one reading in calm.json (atomic) and return calm_since: the time of the first reading of the current
    unbroken calm run, or None. A hot reading clears it; so does a gap over CALM_GAP_S since the last reading
    (nobody saw the machine in between, so calm was not observed). The read-modify-write holds an flock on a
    sibling lock file, so a hot reading by one process is not overwritten by another's stale calm one."""
    try:
        STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        lock = open(STATE_DIR / "calm.lock", "a")
    except OSError:
        return None  # an unwritable state dir only means the boost never accrues: fail toward waiting
    with lock:
        try:
            import fcntl
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        except (ImportError, OSError):
            locked = False
        else:
            locked = True
        if not locked and calm:
            return None  # a calm reading that cannot be serialized could restore a superseded run: toward waiting
        s = calm_load()
        since, last = s.get("calm_since"), s.get("last_t")
        if _num(last) and t < last:
            # an older observation arriving after a newer one (the sampler stamps before it reads, admit after): a calm
            # one changes nothing and never moves last_t back; a hot one still clears the run
            if calm:
                return since if _num(since) else None
            since, t = None, last
        elif not calm:
            since = None
        elif not (_num(since) and _num(last) and 0 <= t - last <= CALM_GAP_S and since <= t):
            since = t
        try:
            tmp = STATE_DIR / f"calm.json.tmp{os.getpid()}"
            tmp.write_text(json.dumps({"calm_since": since, "last_t": t}))
            tmp.replace(STATE_DIR / "calm.json")
        except OSError:
            return None
    return since


def _res_read():
    try:
        r = json.loads((STATE_DIR / "agent-reservations.json").read_text()).get("r", [])
        return [x for x in r if isinstance(x, dict) and isinstance(x.get("id"), str) and _num(x.get("until"))]
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return []


def reservations_active(now_t=None):
    """Number of unexpired agent reservations (an unlocked read: it only reports; `agent_reserve` decides)."""
    now_t = now() if now_t is None else now_t
    return sum(1 for x in _res_read() if x["until"] > now_t)


def _res_locked(fn):
    """Run fn() holding the exclusive flock on agent-reservations.lock; None when the lock cannot be taken."""
    try:
        import fcntl
        STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(STATE_DIR / "agent-reservations.lock", "a") as lock:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            return fn()
    except (ImportError, OSError):
        return None


def _res_write(rows):
    tmp = STATE_DIR / f"agent-reservations.json.tmp{os.getpid()}"
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps({"r": rows}))
    tmp.replace(STATE_DIR / "agent-reservations.json")


def agent_reserve(cap, live, ttl):
    """Atomically admit one more agent: under an flock, count the live acp-run processes (`live`: a number, or a
    callable re-read inside the lock) plus the unexpired reservations; at or above `cap` it refuses, else it records
    a reservation. Returns (None, id) when reserved, else (refusal name, None): `agents`, `agents_unreadable` when ps
    fails, `agents_reserve_failed` when the state cannot be written or locked (fail toward waiting)."""
    def work():
        try:
            n = live() if callable(live) else live
        except ReadFailed:
            return "agents_unreadable", None
        t = now()
        keep = [x for x in _res_read() if x["until"] > t]
        if (n or 0) + len(keep) >= cap:
            return "agents", None
        rid = f"{os.getpid()}-{int(t * 1000)}-{random.randrange(1 << 32):08x}"
        try:
            _res_write(keep + [{"id": rid, "until": t + ttl}])
        except OSError:
            return "agents_reserve_failed", None
        return None, rid

    out = _res_locked(work)
    return out if out is not None else ("agents_reserve_failed", None)


def release_reservation(rid):
    """Shorten reservation `rid` to RELEASE_GRACE_S from now (its agent is spawned, or the launch was refused): the live
    count takes over, and the grace covers the seconds before acp-run shows in ps. True when it was found."""
    def work():
        t = now()
        rows, hit = [], False
        for x in _res_read():
            if x["id"] == rid:
                hit, x = True, {"id": rid, "until": min(x["until"], t + RELEASE_GRACE_S)}
            if x["until"] > t:
                rows.append(x)
        try:
            _res_write(rows)
        except OSError:
            return False
        return hit

    return bool(_res_locked(work))


def renew_reservation(rid):
    """Push reservation `rid` out to LW_RESERVE_S from now (never shortening it): a dispatcher that is still waiting for
    capacity, or for its agent to become countable, keeps its place however long that takes. False when it is gone
    (released or expired: a reservation that lapsed is not resurrected, the dispatcher is told so)."""
    def work():
        t = now()
        rows, hit = [], False
        for x in _res_read():
            if x["until"] <= t:
                continue
            if x["id"] == rid:
                hit, x = True, {"id": rid, "until": max(x["until"], t + ADMIT_RESERVE_S)}
            rows.append(x)
        try:
            _res_write(rows)
        except OSError:
            return False
        return hit

    return bool(_res_locked(work))


def cmd_renew(a):
    ok = renew_reservation(a.id)
    print(f"renewed {a.id}" if ok else f"no reservation {a.id}")
    return 0 if ok else 1


def cmd_release(a):
    ok = release_reservation(a.id)
    print(f"released {a.id}" if ok else f"no reservation {a.id}")
    return 0 if ok else 1


def admit_refusals(per_core, limit, m, lim):
    """Names of the gates that refuse: load, compressor, free_mem, pageins, agents, and `memory_unreadable` /
    `agents_unreadable` (vm_stat or ps exists but the read failed or timed out: that is likeliest exactly when the
    machine is starving, so it refuses). A reading whose tool is absent altogether (None, no failure) never
    refuses; it is reported as `unreadable`. The agent cap 0 is off."""
    out = []
    if per_core > limit:
        out.append("load")
    if m["churn"] is not None and m["churn"] > lim["churn"]:
        out.append("compressor")
    if m["free_mb"] is not None and m["free_mb"] < lim["min_free_mb"]:
        out.append("free_mem")
    if m["pageins_s"] is not None and m["pageins_s"] > lim["max_pageins"]:
        out.append("pageins")
    if lim["max_agents"] and m["agents"] is not None and m["agents"] + m.get("reserved", 0) >= lim["max_agents"]:
        out.append("agents")
    if "memory" in m["failed"]:
        out.append("memory_unreadable")
    if "agents" in m["failed"] and lim["max_agents"]:
        out.append("agents_unreadable")
    out.extend(x for x in m.get("extra", []) if x not in out)  # refusals decided at the reservation step
    return out


def admit_record(load1, cores, per_core, limit, waited, m, lim, calm_for=None):
    """The admit result fields; adds the watcher's streak and hot_for_s when its state.json is fresh."""
    refused = admit_refusals(per_core, limit, m, lim)
    rec = {"status": "hot" if refused else "ok", "load1": round(load1, 2),
           "per_core": round(per_core, 2), "cores": cores, "max_per_core": limit, "waited_s": int(waited)}
    if refused:
        rec["refused"] = refused
    if m["churn"] is not None:
        rec["mem_churn_pages_s"] = int(m["churn"])
        rec["max_mem_churn_pages_s"] = lim["churn"]
    if m["free_mb"] is not None:
        rec["free_mb"] = int(m["free_mb"])
        rec["min_free_mb"] = lim["min_free_mb"]
    if m["pageins_s"] is not None:
        rec["pageins_s"] = int(m["pageins_s"])
        rec["max_pageins_s"] = lim["max_pageins"]
    if m["agents"] is not None:
        rec["agents"] = m["agents"]
        if m.get("reserved"):
            rec["reserved"] = m["reserved"]
    if m.get("reservation") and not refused:
        rec["reservation"] = m["reservation"]
    rec["max_agents"] = lim["max_agents"]
    cap_on = bool(lim["max_agents"])
    unreadable = [name for k, name in (("churn", "memory"), ("agents", "agents"))
                  if m[k] is None and name not in m["failed"] and (k == "churn" or cap_on)]
    if unreadable:
        rec["unreadable"] = unreadable
    if calm_for is not None:
        rec["calm_for_s"] = int(calm_for)
    rec.update(watcher_fields())
    return rec


def _num(x):
    return isinstance(x, (int, float)) and not isinstance(x, bool) and math.isfinite(x)


def watcher_fields():
    """streak and hot_for_s from the watcher's state.json, only when it is a dict with numeric, fresh `t` and
    `hot_since`; anything else (a list, a string time, a torn write) is "no state", never an error: a crash here
    used to end a wait that had measured a hot machine."""
    try:
        st = load_state()
        if not isinstance(st, dict) or not (_num(st.get("t")) and _num(st.get("hot_since"))):
            return {}
        if abs(now() - st["t"]) > ADMIT_FRESH_S:
            return {}
        streak = st.get("streak", 0)
        return {"streak": int(streak) if _num(streak) else 0, "hot_for_s": int(max(0.0, now() - st["hot_since"]))}
    except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError, RecursionError):
        return {}


def admit_line(rec):
    line = f"admit {rec['status']} load1={rec['load1']:g} per_core={rec['per_core']:.2f} cores={rec['cores']}"
    if "mem_churn_pages_s" in rec:
        line += f" mem_churn={rec['mem_churn_pages_s']}"
    if "free_mb" in rec:
        line += f" free_mb={rec['free_mb']}"
    if "pageins_s" in rec:
        line += f" pageins={rec['pageins_s']}"
    if "agents" in rec:
        line += f" agents={rec['agents']}"
    if "unreadable" in rec:
        line += " unreadable=" + ",".join(rec["unreadable"]) + " (gate open: reading failed)"
    if rec["status"] == "hot":
        line += " refused=" + ",".join(rec["refused"])
        if "load" in rec["refused"]:
            line += f" max_per_core={rec['max_per_core']:g}"
        if "compressor" in rec["refused"]:
            line += f" max_mem_churn={rec['max_mem_churn_pages_s']:g}"
        if "free_mem" in rec["refused"]:
            line += f" min_free_mb={rec['min_free_mb']:g}"
        if "pageins" in rec["refused"]:
            line += f" max_pageins={rec['max_pageins_s']:g}"
        if "agents" in rec["refused"]:
            line += f" max_agents={rec['max_agents']}"
    if rec.get("reservation"):
        line += f" reservation={rec['reservation']} (release it: load-watch release {rec['reservation']}; --no-reserve to only check)"
    if "hot_for_s" in rec:
        line += f" streak={rec['streak']} hot_for_s={rec['hot_for_s']}"
    if rec["waited_s"]:
        line += f" waited_s={rec['waited_s']}"
    return line


def cmd_admit(a):
    """May new work start now? Only ever decides; never kills, throttles or signals anything."""
    lim = {"churn": getattr(a, "max_mem_churn", ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S), "min_free_mb": getattr(a, "min_free_mb", ADMIT_MIN_FREE_MB),
           "max_pageins": getattr(a, "max_pageins", ADMIT_PAGEINS_S), "max_agents": getattr(a, "max_agents", 0)}
    if (not (math.isfinite(a.wait) and math.isfinite(a.max_per_core) and all(math.isfinite(v) for v in lim.values()))
            or a.wait < 0 or a.max_per_core <= 0 or lim["churn"] <= 0 or lim["max_pageins"] <= 0
            or lim["min_free_mb"] < 0 or lim["max_agents"] < 0):
        print("load-watch admit: --wait must be a finite number, 0 or more, --max-per-core, --max-mem-churn and "
              "--max-pageins finite and above 0, --min-free-mb and --max-agents 0 or more", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        lo, hi = (float(x) for x in os.environ.get("LW_ADMIT_STAGGER_S", "5,30").split(","))
        poll = float(os.environ.get("LW_ADMIT_POLL_S", "15"))
        fake, fake_churn, fake_mem = _fake_loads(), _fake_churn(), _fake_memory()
        if not (math.isfinite(lo) and math.isfinite(hi) and math.isfinite(poll) and 0 <= lo <= hi <= 60
                and all(math.isfinite(x) for x in fake + fake_churn + sum(fake_mem.values(), []))):
            raise ValueError("out of range")
    except ValueError:
        print("load-watch admit: bad LW_FAKE_LOAD1, LW_FAKE_CHURN, LW_FAKE_FREE_MB, LW_FAKE_PAGEINS, LW_FAKE_AGENTS, "
              "LW_ADMIT_POLL_S or LW_ADMIT_STAGGER_S (finite, stagger 0 <= min <= max <= 60)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    poll = max(1.0, poll)  # never a busy loop on a machine that is already hot
    boost = getattr(a, "boost_per_core", ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE)
    boost_churn = getattr(a, "boost_max_churn", ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S)
    if not (math.isfinite(boost) and math.isfinite(boost_churn)) or boost < 0 or boost_churn <= 0:
        print("load-watch admit: --boost-per-core and --boost-max-churn must be finite (0 turns the boost off)",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if fake and not fake_churn:
        boost = 0  # a faked load with no faked churn reads churn 0 (not a measurement): never boosts
    measured = not fake or bool(fake_churn) or any(fake_mem.values())  # a defaulted fake reading is not an observation
    reserve_on = bool(lim["max_agents"]) and ADMIT_RESERVE_S > 0 and not getattr(a, "no_reserve", False)  # records one

    def read(polls):
        load1, cores, per_core = admit_reading(fake, polls)
        m = admit_memory(fake, fake_churn, fake_mem, polls, lim["max_agents"])
        if lim["max_agents"]:
            m["reserved"] = reservations_active() if ADMIT_RESERVE_S > 0 else 0   # counted whenever the cap is evaluated, reserving or not
        calm_for = None
        if measured:  # every real reading feeds the shared clock, boost or not (a hot one must reset it for everyone)
            t = now()
            # judged with the module defaults only: one caller's loose flags must not start the shared calm clock for others
            since = calm_note(t, memory_calm(m["churn"], m["free_mb"], m["pageins_s"]))
            if boost and boost > a.max_per_core:
                calm_for = (t - since) if since is not None else None
        # the boost needs an unbroken calm run of at least ADMIT_BOOST_CALM_S (churn None: no boost either)
        limit = admit_limit(a.max_per_core, m["churn"] if calm_for is not None and calm_for >= ADMIT_BOOST_CALM_S else None,
                            boost, boost_churn)
        return load1, cores, per_core, m, limit, calm_for

    start, polls, next_note = time.monotonic(), 0, 60.0
    while True:
        load1, cores, per_core, m, limit, calm_for = read(polls)
        polls += 1
        waited = time.monotonic() - start
        if not admit_refusals(per_core, limit, m, lim) and polls > 1:
            # the load fell while we waited: stagger so queued dispatchers do not all start in the same second,
            # then look again (someone else may have started in the meantime)
            # (never past the --wait budget: deferred records and rearm timeouts only budget that much)
            left = a.wait - waited
            if left > 0:
                time.sleep(min(random.uniform(lo, hi), left))
            load1, cores, per_core, m, limit, calm_for = read(polls)
            polls += 1
            waited = time.monotonic() - start
        refused = admit_refusals(per_core, limit, m, lim)
        if not refused and reserve_on:
            live = m["agents"] if (fake or fake_churn or any(fake_mem.values())) else count_agents
            why, rid = agent_reserve(lim["max_agents"], live, ADMIT_RESERVE_S)
            if why:
                m["extra"] = [why]
                refused = admit_refusals(per_core, limit, m, lim)
            else:
                m["reservation"] = rid
        if not refused or waited >= a.wait:
            break
        if waited >= next_note:
            print(f"load-watch admit: waiting, refused={','.join(refused)} load1={load1:g} per_core={per_core:.2f} (limit {limit:g})"
                  + (f" mem_churn={m['churn']:.0f} (limit {lim['churn']:g})" if m["churn"] is not None else "")
                  + (f" free_mb={m['free_mb']:.0f} (floor {lim['min_free_mb']:g})" if m["free_mb"] is not None else "")
                  + (f" pageins={m['pageins_s']:.0f} (limit {lim['max_pageins']:g})" if m["pageins_s"] is not None else "")
                  + (f" agents={m['agents']} (cap {lim['max_agents']})" if m["agents"] is not None else "")
                  + f", {int(waited)}s of {a.wait:g}s", file=sys.stderr)
            next_note += 60.0
        time.sleep(max(0.0, min(poll, a.wait - waited)))
    rec = admit_record(load1, cores, per_core, limit, waited, m, lim, calm_for)
    print(json.dumps(rec) if a.json else admit_line(rec))
    return 0 if rec["status"] == "ok" else EX_TEMPFAIL


def cmd_install(a):
    dest = HOME / "Library/LaunchAgents" / PLIST.name
    dom = f"gui/{os.getuid()}"
    subprocess.run(["launchctl", "bootout", f"{dom}/{LABEL}"], capture_output=True)
    if a.cmd == "uninstall":
        dest.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        print(f"removed {dest}")
        return 0
    STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = dest.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(PLIST.read_text())
    tmp.replace(dest)
    r = subprocess.run(["launchctl", "bootstrap", dom, str(dest)], capture_output=True, text=True)
    print(f"installed {dest}" if r.returncode == 0 else f"bootstrap failed: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return r.returncode


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    p = sub.add_parser("sample")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="attribute and print; no brief, relay, ping or cooldown")
    p.add_argument("-v", "--verbose", action="store_true")
    sub.add_parser("status")
    p = sub.add_parser("incidents")
    p.add_argument("-n", type=int, default=20)
    p = sub.add_parser("ack")
    p.add_argument("id")
    p.add_argument("note")
    p = sub.add_parser("ci-only")
    p.add_argument("op", choices=["list", "add", "rm", "check"])
    p.add_argument("dir", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("ci_cmd", nargs="?", metavar="CMD")
    p = sub.add_parser("guard")
    p.add_argument("op", choices=["status", "list", "add", "rm", "reset"])
    p.add_argument("label", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("limits", nargs="*", metavar="KEY=VALUE")
    p.add_argument("--note")
    p = sub.add_parser("ci")
    p.add_argument("op", choices=["list", "check", "decide", "rm"])
    p.add_argument("dir", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("mode", nargs="?", choices=MODES)
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?", metavar="CMD_OR_REASON")
    p = sub.add_parser("renew")
    p.add_argument("id", metavar="RESERVATION", help="extend an agent reservation by LW_RESERVE_S from now")
    p = sub.add_parser("release")
    p.add_argument("id", metavar="RESERVATION", help="the `reservation` id an `admit --max-agents --json` printed")
    p = sub.add_parser("admit")
    p.add_argument("--max-per-core", type=float, default=ADMIT_PER_CORE, metavar="N",
                   help=f"admit when 1-minute load per core is at most N (default {ADMIT_PER_CORE:g})")
    p.add_argument("--max-mem-churn", type=float, default=ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S, metavar="N",
                   help=f"and compressor churn (pages compressed + decompressed per second, sampled over ~{ADMIT_MEM_WINDOW_S:g} s) "
                        f"is at most N (default {ADMIT_CHURN_PAGES_S:g}, env LW_MAX_COMPRESSOR_S; was 60000 until 2026-11-01)")
    p.add_argument("--min-free-mb", type=float, default=ADMIT_MIN_FREE_MB, metavar="N",
                   help=f"and free+speculative memory is at least N MB (default {ADMIT_MIN_FREE_MB:g}, env LW_MIN_FREE_MB)")
    p.add_argument("--max-pageins", type=float, default=ADMIT_PAGEINS_S, metavar="N",
                   help=f"and pageins per second are at most N (default {ADMIT_PAGEINS_S:g}, env LW_MAX_PAGEINS_S)")
    p.add_argument("--max-agents", type=int, nargs="?", const=ADMIT_MAX_AGENTS, default=0, metavar="N",
                   help=f"and fewer than N `acp-run` agent sessions are alive machine-wide. OFF unless given (0 = off), because "
                        f"only a caller that STARTS agents (acp-dispatch) may be gated by it; `bg` test runs must never be. "
                        f"Bare `--max-agents` means {ADMIT_MAX_AGENTS} (env LW_MAX_AGENTS; 0 there = off)")
    p.add_argument("--no-reserve", action="store_true",
                   help=f"with --max-agents, do not record a reservation for an admission (a pure check); otherwise an "
                        f"admission counts as one agent for LW_RESERVE_S ({ADMIT_RESERVE_S:g}) seconds, so concurrent "
                        f"dispatchers cannot all be admitted under the cap")
    p.add_argument("--boost-per-core", type=float, default=ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE, metavar="N",
                   help=f"while churn is at most --boost-max-churn, admit up to N per core instead "
                        f"(default {ADMIT_BOOST_PER_CORE:g}; 0 turns the boost off)")
    p.add_argument("--boost-max-churn", type=float, default=ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S, metavar="N",
                   help=f"the churn (pages/s) up to which the boost applies (default {ADMIT_BOOST_CHURN_PAGES_S:g})")
    p.add_argument("--wait", type=float, default=0, metavar="SECONDS",
                   help="poll every 15 s for up to SECONDS before giving up with exit 75 (0: a pure check)")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("watcher", help="the one agent session that hears about every spike (loadwatch skill)")
    p.add_argument("op", choices=["set", "show", "clear", "test"])
    p.add_argument("target", nargs="?", help="clear: only if it is this target; test: the text to send")
    p.add_argument("--paseo", metavar="AGENT_ID", help="set: a Paseo agent (default: $PASEO_AGENT_ID)")
    p.add_argument("--relay", metavar="TARGET", help="set: a relay.py target (default: $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID)")
    p.add_argument("--sid", help="set: the agent's own session id, kept for matching")
    p.add_argument("--name", help="set: a label for the session")
    p.add_argument("--cwd", help="set: the session's directory (default: the current one)")
    p.add_argument("--chain", help="set: its session-handoff chain, for /baton")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="show: the record as JSON")
    sub.add_parser("install")
    sub.add_parser("uninstall")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.cmd is None:
        ap.print_usage(sys.stderr)
        return 2
    return {"sample": cmd_sample, "status": cmd_status, "incidents": cmd_incidents, "ack": cmd_ack,
            "guard": cmd_guard, "watcher": cmd_watcher, "admit": cmd_admit, "release": cmd_release, "renew": cmd_renew, "ci": cmd_ci, "ci-only": cmd_ci_only, "install": cmd_install, "uninstall": cmd_install}[a.cmd](a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
